{
  "title": "7: al-Aa'raaf الأعراف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالۤمّۤصۤ‏(1)\nAM-MS.\nAlif, Lam, Mim, Sad. \nكِتٰبٌ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ فَلَا يَكُنْ فِىْ صَدْرِكَ حَرَجٌ مِّنْهُ لِتُنْذِرَ بِهٖ وَذِكْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(2)\nKETAABUM UNZELA ELAYKA FALAA YAKUL FEE SADREKA HARAJUN MINHO LETUNZERA BEHI WAZEKRAA LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nA Book revealed unto thee, So let thy heart be oppressed no more by any difficulty on that account, that with it thou mightest warn (the erring) and teach the Believers). \nاِتَّبِعُوْا مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَلَا تَتَّبِعُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(3)\nAETTABEU’OOA MAA UNZELA ELAYKUM MIN RABBEKUM WA LAA TATTABE-O’O MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA QALEELAA MAA TAZAKKAROON.\nFollow (O men!) the revelation given unto you from your Lord, and follow not, as friends or protectors, other than Him. Little it is ye remember of admonition. \nوَكَمْ مِّنْ قَرْيَةٍ اَهْلَكْنٰهَا فَجَآءَهَا بَاْسُنَا بَيَاتًا اَوْ هُمْ قَآئِلُوْنَ‏(4)\nWA MIN QARYATINW AAHLAKNAAHAA FA JAAA-AHAA BAASUNAA BAYAATAN AW HUM QAAELOONA.\nHow many towns have We destroyed (for their sins)? Our punishment took them on a sudden by night or while they slept for their afternoon rest. \nفَمَا كَانَ دَعْوٰٮهُمْ اِذْ جَآءَهُمْ بَاْسُنَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(5)\nFAMAA KAANA DAA’WAAHUM IZ JAAA-AHUM BAASUNAA ILLAA AN QAALOO INNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nWhen (thus) Our punishment took them, no cry did they utter but this: “Indeed we did wrong.” \nفَلَنَسْئَلَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اُرْسِلَ اِلَيْهِمْ وَلَنَسْئَلَنَّ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ ۙ‏(6)\nFALANASALANNA LAZEENA AURSELA ELAYHIM WALANASALANNA MURSALEEN.\nThen shall we question those to whom Our message was sent and those by whom We sent it. \nفَلَنَقُصَّنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ بِعِلْمٍ وَّمَا كُنَّا غَآئِبِيْنَ‏(7)\nFALANAQUSSANNA A’LAYHIM BE-I’LMIN WA MAA KUNNAA GHAAEBEENA.\nAnd verily, We shall recount their whole story with knowledge, for We were never absent (at any time or place). \nوَالْوَزْنُ يَوْمَئِذِ اۨلْحَقُّ ۚ فَمَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(8)\nWAL WAZNU YAWMAEZE HAQQO FAMAN SAQOLAT MAWAAZEENOHU FAAWLAAEKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThe balance that day will be true (to nicety): those whose scale (of good) will be heavy, will prosper: \nوَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(9)\nWA MAN KHAFFAT MAWAAZEENOHU FAAWLAAEKA LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM BEMAA KAANOO BE-AAYAATENAA YAZLEMOON.\nThose whose scale will be light, will be their souls in perdition, for that they wrongfully treated Our signs. \nوَلَقَدْ مَكَّنّٰكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَجَعَلْنَا لَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَعَايِشَ ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(10)\nWA LAQAD MAKKANNAAKUM FIL ARZE WA JA-A’LNAA LAKUM FEEHAA MAA’AAYESHA QALEELAA MAA TASHKOROON.\nIt is We Who have placed you with authority on earth, and provided you therein with means for the fulfilment of your life: small are the thanks that ye give! \nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنٰكُمْ ثُمَّ صَوَّرْنٰكُمْ ثُمَّ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰۤئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ ۖ  فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ لَمْ يَكُنْ مِّنَ السّٰجِدِيْنَ‏(11)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAAKUM SUMMA SAWRNAAKUM SUMMA QULNAL LIL-MALAAEKATE JODOO LE-AADAMA FASAJADOOA ILLAA IBLEES LAM YAKUL MENAL AS-SAAJEDEENA.\nIt is We Who created you and gave you shape; then We bade the angels prostrate to Adam, and they prostrate; not so Iblis; He refused to be of those who prostrate. \nقَالَ مَا مَنَعَكَ اَلَّا تَسْجُدَ اِذْ اَمَرْتُكَ ؕ قَالَ اَنَا خَيْرٌ مِّنْهُ ۚ خَلَقْتَنِىْ مِنْ نَّارٍ وَّخَلَقْتَهٗ مِنْ طِيْنٍ‏(12)\nQAALA MAA MANAA’AKA ALLAA TASJUDA IZ AAMARTUKA QAALA ANAA KHAYRUL MINHO KHALAQTANEAA MIN NAAR WWAKHALAQTAH MIN TEENIN.\n(Allah) said: “What prevented thee from prostrating when I commanded thee?” He said: “I am better than he: Thou didst create me from fire, and him from clay.” \nقَالَ فَاهْبِطْ مِنْهَا فَمَا يَكُوْنُ لَكَ اَنْ تَتَكَبَّرَ فِيْهَا فَاخْرُجْ اِنَّكَ مِنَ الصّٰغِرِيْنَ‏(13)\nQAALA FAAHBET MINHAA FAMAA LAHUL LAKA AN TATAKABBARA FEEHAA FAKHRUJ INNAKA MENAL AS-SAAGHEREENA.\n(Allah) said: “Get thee down from this: it is not for thee to be arrogant here: get out, for thou art of the meanest (of creatures).” \nقَالَ اَنْظِرْنِىْۤ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(14)\nQAALA AANZERNEAA ELAA YAWMIL YUB-A’SOON.\nHe said: “Give me respite till the day they are raised up.” \nقَالَ اِنَّكَ مِنَ الْمُنْظَرِيْنَ‏(15)\nQAALA INNAKA MENAL AL-MUNZAREENA.\n(Allah) said: “Be thou among those who have respite.” \nقَالَ فَبِمَاۤ اَغْوَيْتَنِىْ لَاَقْعُدَنَّ لَهُمْ صِرَاطَكَ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَۙ‏(16)\nQAALA FA BEMAA AAGHWAYTANEAA LAAQU’UDANNA LAHUM SERAATAKA AL-MUSTAQEEMA.\nHe said: “Because thou hast thrown me out of the way, lo! I will lie in wait for them on thy straight way: \nثُمَّ لَاَتِيَنَّهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَيْنِ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ وَعَنْ اَيْمَانِهِمْ وَعَنْ شَمَآئِلِهِمْؕ وَلَاٰ تَجِدُ اَكْثَرَهُمْ شٰكِرِيْنَ‏(17)\nSUMMA LAATEENNAHUM MIN BAYNE AYDEEHIM WA MIN KHALFEHIM WA A’N AAYMAANEHEM WA A’N SHAMAAELEHEM WALAA TAJEDU AKSARAHUM SHAAKEREENA.\n“Then will I assault them from before them and behind them, from their right and their left: Nor wilt thou find, in most of them, gratitude (for thy mercies).” \nقَالَ اخْرُجْ مِنْهَا مَذْءُوْمًا مَّدْحُوْرًا ؕ لَمَنْ تَبِعَكَ مِنْهُمْ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنْكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(18)\nQAALA AKHRUJ MINHAA MAZOOMAN MMADHOORAN LAMAN TABEA’AKA MINHUM LAAMLAANNA JAHANNAMA MINKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\n(Allah) said: “Get out from this, disgraced and expelled. If any of them follow thee, Hell will I fill with you all. \nوَيٰۤاٰدَمُ اسْكُنْ اَنْتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ فَكُلَا مِنْ حَيْثُ شِئْتُمَا وَلَا تَقْرَبَا هٰذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُوْنَا مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(19)\nWAYAAADAMU AADAMUS ANTA WA ZAWJOKAL JANNATA FAKULAA MIN HAYSO SHEATOMAA WA LAA TAQRABAA HAAZEHE SHAJARATA FA-TAKOONAA MENAL ZAALEMEEN.\n“O Adam! dwell thou and thy wife in the Garden, and enjoy (its good things) as ye wish: but approach not this tree, or ye run into harm and transgression.” \nفَوَسْوَسَ لَهُمَا الشَّيْطٰنُ لِيُبْدِىَ لَهُمَا مَا وٗرِىَ عَنْهُمَا مِنْ سَوْاٰتِهِمَا وَقَالَ مَا نَهٰٮكُمَا رَبُّكُمَا عَنْ هٰذِهِ الشَّجَرَةِ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ تَكُوْنَا مَلَكَيْنِ اَوْ تَكُوْنَا مِنَ الْخٰلِدِيْنَ‏(20)\nFAWASWASA LAHOMAA SHAYTAANO LEEBDEAAA LAHOMAA MAA WREAAA A’ANHUMAA MIN SAWAAATEHEMAA WA QAALA MAA NAHAAKUMAA RABBUKUMAA A’N HAAZEHE SHAJARATE ILLAA AN TAKOONAA MALAKAYNE AW TAKOONAA MENAL AL-KHAALEDEENA.\nThen began Satan to whisper suggestions to them, bringing openly before their minds all their shame that was hidden from them (before): he said: “Your Lord only forbade you this tree, lest ye should become angels or such beings as live for ever.” \nوَقَاسَمَهُمَاۤ اِنِّىْ لَكُمَا لَمِنَ النّٰصِحِيْنَۙ‏(21)\nWAQAASAMAHUMAA INNEE LAKOMAA LAMENAS NAASEHEEN.\nAnd he swore to them both, that he was their sincere adviser. \nفَدَلّٰٮهُمَا بِغُرُوْرٍ ۚ فَلَمَّا ذَاقَا الشَّجَرَةَ بَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْءٰتُهُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفٰنِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِنْ وَّرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ ؕ وَنَادٰٮهُمَا رَبُّهُمَاۤ اَلَمْ اَنْهَكُمَا عَنْ تِلْكُمَا الشَّجَرَةِ وَاَقُلْ لَّكُمَاۤ اِنَّ الشَّيْطٰنَ لَكُمَا عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(22)\nFADALLAAHUMAA BE-GHOROOR FALAMMAA ZAAQAA SHAJARATA BADAT LAHOMAA SAWAATUHUMAA WATAFEQAA YAKHSEFAANE FEEMAF MIN WWARAQE JANNAH WANAADAAHUMAA RABBUHUMAA ALAM AANHAKUMAA A’N TELKUMAA SHAJARATE WAAQUL LLAKUMAA INNAL ASH-SHAYTAANA LAKOMAA A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nSo by deceit he brought about their fall: when they tasted of the tree, their shame became manifest to them, and they began to sew together the leaves of the garden over their bodies. And their Lord called unto them: “Did I not forbid you that tree, and tell you that Satan was an avowed enemy unto you?” \nقَالَا رَبَّنَا ظَلَمْنَاۤ اَنْفُسَنَا وَاِنْ لَّمْ تَغْفِرْ لَنَا وَتَرْحَمْنَا لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(23)\nQAALAA RABBANAA ZALAMNAA AANFUSANAA WA LAM TAGHFER LANAA WATARHAMNAA LANAKOONANNA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nThey said: “Our Lord! We have wronged our own souls: If thou forgive us not and bestow not upon us Thy Mercy, we shall certainly be lost.” \nقَالَ اهْبِطُوْا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ ۚ وَلَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَّمَتَاعٌ اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(24)\nQAALA BETOO BA’ZOKUM LE-BA’ZIN A’DUWWUM WA LAKUM FIL ARZE MUSTAQARRUNW WA MATAA-U’N ELAA HEEN.\n(Allah) said: “Get ye down. With enmity between yourselves. On earth will be your dwelling-place and your means of livelihood, for a time.” \nقَالَ فِيْهَا تَحْيَوْنَ وَفِيْهَا تَمُوْتُوْنَ وَمِنْهَا تُخْرَجُوْنَ‏(25)\nQAALA FEEHAA TAHYAWNA WA FEEHAA TAMOOTOONA WA MINHAA TUKHRAJOON.\nHe said: “Therein shall ye live, and therein shall ye die; but from it shall ye be taken out (at last).” \nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ قَدْ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمْ لِبَاسًا يُّوَارِىْ سَوْاٰتِكُمْ وَرِيْشًا ؕ وَلِبَاسُ التَّقْوٰى ۙ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(26)\nYAA BANEE AADAMAL QAD ANZALNAA A’LAYKUM LEBAASANW YYOOAREAA SAWAAATEKUM WAREESHAN WALEBAASU TAQWAA ZAA LEKA KHAYRUL ZAA LEKA MIN AAYAATIL LAAHE LA-A’LLAHUM YAZZAKKAROONA.\nO ye Children of Adam! We have bestowed raiment upon you to cover your shame, as well as to be an adornment to you. But the raiment of righteousness, that is the best. Such are among the Signs of Allah, that they may receive admonition! \nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ لَا يَفْتِنَنَّكُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ كَمَاۤ اَخْرَجَ اَبَوَيْكُمْ مِّنَ الْجَنَّةِ يَنْزِعُ عَنْهُمَا لِبَاسَهُمَا لِيُرِيَهُمَا سَوْءاٰتِهِمَا ؕ اِنَّهٗ يَرٰٮكُمْ هُوَ وَقَبِيْلُهٗ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا تَرَوْنَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّا جَعَلْنَا الشَّيٰطِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ لِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(27)\nYAA BANEE AADAMAL LAA YAFTENANNAKUMU SHAYTAANO KAMAA AKHRAJAL AABAWAYKUM MENAL JANNAH YANZEU’U A’ANHUMAA LEBAASAHUMAA LEEREEHUMAA SAWAAATEHEMAA INNAHU YARAAKUM HOWA WAQABEELUH MIN HAYSO LAA TARAWNAHUM INNAA JA-A’LNAA SHAYAATEENA AAWLEEAAAA LILLAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA.\nO ye Children of Adam! Let not Satan seduce you, in the same manner as He got your parents out of the Garden, stripping them of their raiment, to expose their shame: for he and his tribe watch you from a position where ye cannot see them: We made the evil ones friends (only) to those without faith. \nوَاِذَا فَعَلُوْا فَاحِشَةً قَالُوْا وَجَدْنَا عَلَيْهَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا وَاللّٰهُ اَمَرَنَا بِهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَاْمُرُ بِالْفَحْشَآءِ ؕ اَتَقُوْلُوْنَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(28)\nWA EZAA FAA’ALOOA FAAHESHATAN QAALOO WAJADNAA A’LAYHAA AABAAA-ANAA WAL LAAHO AAMARANAA BEHAA QUL INNAL LAAHA LAA YAAMURU BIL-FAHSHAAA AATAQOOLOONA A’LAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nWhen they do aught that is shameful, they say: “We found our fathers doing so”; and “Allah commanded us thus”: Say: “Nay, Allah never commands what is shameful: do ye say of Allah what ye know not?” \nقُلْ اَمَرَ رَبِّىْ بِالْقِسْطِ وَاَقِيْمُوْا وُجُوْهَكُمْ عِنْدَ كُلِّ مَسْجِدٍ وَّادْعُوْهُ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ    ؕ كَمَا بَدَاَكُمْ تَعُوْدُوْنَؕ‏(29)\nQUL AMARAL RABBEE BIL QISTE WAAQEEMOOA WOJOOHAKUM I’NDAL KULLE MASJEDIN WWAADU’OOHU MUKHLESEENA LAHUL DEENA KAMAA BADAAKUM TAU’OODOONA.\nSay: “My Lord hath commanded justice; and that ye set your whole selves (to Him) at every time and place of prayer, and call upon Him, making your devotion sincere as in His sight: such as He created you in the beginning, so shall ye return.” \nفَرِيْقًا هَدٰى وَ فَرِيْقًا حَقَّ عَلَيْهِمُ الضَّلٰلَةُ  ؕ اِنَّهُمُ اتَّخَذُوا الشَّيٰطِيْنَ اَوْلِيَآءَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ وَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ مُّهْتَدُوْنَ‏(30)\nFAREEQAM HADAA WA FAREEQAM HAQQA A’LAYHEMUL AZ-ZALAALATU AENNAHUMU ATTAKHAZOOA SHAYAATEENA AAWLEEAAAA MIN DOONIL LAAHE WA YAHSABOONAL ANNAHUM HUM MOHTADOON.\nSome He hath guided: Others have (by their choice) deserved the loss of their way; in that they took the evil ones, in preference to Allah, for their friends and protectors, and think that they receive guidance. \nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ خُذُوْا زِيْنَتَكُمْ عِنْدَ كُلِّ مَسْجِدٍ وَّكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا وَلَا تُسْرِفُوْا ۚ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِيْنَ‏(31)\nYAA BANEE AADAMAL KHOZOO ZEENATAKUM I’NDAL KULLE MASJEDIN WWAKULOOA WASH RABOO WA LAA TUSREFOOA INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL MUSREFEEN.\n O Children of Adam! wear your beautiful apparel at every time and place of prayer: eat and drink: But waste not by excess, for Allah loveth not the wasters. \nقُلْ مَنْ حَرَّمَ زِيْنَةَ اللّٰهِ الَّتِىْۤ اَخْرَجَ لِعِبَادِهٖ وَالطَّيِّبٰتِ مِنَ الرِّزْقِؕ قُلْ هِىَ لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا خَالِصَةً يَّوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّعْلَمُوْنَ‏(32)\nQUL MAN HARRAMA ZEENATA LAAHE LATEE AKHRAJAL LE-E’BAADEHI WAALTTAYBAATE MENAL AR-REZQE QUL HEYA LILLAZEENA AAMANOO FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA KHAALESATAM YAWMA AL-QEEMATE KAZAALEKA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YA’LAMOON.\nSay: Who hath forbidden the beautiful (gifts) of Allah, which He hath produced for His servants, and the things, clean and pure, (which He hath provided) for sustenance? Say: They are, in the life of this world, for those who believe, (and) purely for them on the Day of Judgment. Thus do We explain the signs in detail for those who understand. \nقُلْ اِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ رَبِّىَ الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ وَ الْاِثْمَ وَالْبَغْىَ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَاَنْ تُشْرِكُوْا بِاللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يُنَزِّلْ بِهٖ سُلْطٰنًا وَّاَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(33)\nQUL INNAMAA HARRAMA RABBEYAL AL-FAWAAHESHA MAA ZAHARAL MINHAA WA MAA BATANA WA AL-AESMA WAL BAGHAAA BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA TUSHREKOOA BIL-LAAHE MAA LAM YUNAZZEL BEHI SULTAANAN WA TAQOOLOO A’LAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\nSay: the things that my Lord hath indeed forbidden are: shameful deeds, whether open or secret; sins and trespasses against truth or reason; assigning of partners to Allah, for which He hath given no authority; and saying things about Allah of which ye have no knowledge. \nوَلِكُلِّ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلٌۚ فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَجَلُهُمْ لَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ سَاعَةً وَّلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA LEKULLIM UMMATIN AJALUM FA-EZAA JAAA-A AAJALUHUM LAA YASTAAKHEROONA SAAA’ATAN WA LAA YASTAQDEMOONA.\nTo every people is a term appointed: when their term is reached, not an hour can they cause delay, nor (an hour) can they advance (it in anticipation). \nيٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ اِمَّا يَاْتِيَنَّكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْكُمْ يَقُصُّوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِىْۙ فَمَنِ اتَّقٰى وَاَصْلَحَ فَلَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(35)\nYAA BANEE AADAMAL IMMAA YAATEYANNAKUM RUSULUN MINKUM YAQUSSOONA A’LAYKUM AAAYAATEAA FAMANE’ WAA WAASLAHA FALAA KHAWFUN A’LAYHIM WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nO ye Children of Adam! whenever there come to you messengers from amongst you, rehearsing My signs unto you, those who are righteous and mend (their lives), on them shall be no fear nor shall they grieve. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا عَنْهَاۤ اُولٰۤئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(36)\nWAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WAASTAKBAROOA A’NHAA AOOLAAEKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nBut those who reject Our signs and treat them with arrogance, they are companions of the Fire, to dwell therein (for ever). \nفَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِاٰيٰتِهٖ ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ يَنَالُهُمْ نَصِيْبُهُمْ مِّنَ الْكِتٰبِؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُنَا يَتَوَفَّوْنَهُمْ ۙ قَالُوْۤا اَيْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ ؕ قَالُوْا ضَلُّوْا عَنَّا وَشَهِدُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ اَنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(37)\nFAMAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW KAZZABA BE-AAYAATEHI AOOLAAEKA YANAALUHUM NASEEBUHUM MENAL AL-KETAABE HATTAA EZAA JAAA-AHUM ROSOLONAA YATAWAFFAWNAHUM QAALOO AYNA MAA KUNTUM TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE QAALOO ZALLOOA WAGH WASHAHEDOOA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM ANNAHUM KAANOO KAAFEREEN.\nWho is more unjust than one who invents a lie against Allah or rejects His Signs? For such, their portion appointed must reach them from the Book (of decrees): until, when our messengers (of death) arrive and take their souls, they say: “Where are the things that ye used to invoke besides Allah?” They will reply, “They have left us in the lurch,” And they will bear witness against themselves, that they had rejected Allah. \nقَالَ ادْخُلُوْا فِىْۤ اُمَمٍ قَدْ خَلَتْ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ فِى النَّارِ ؕ كُلَّمَا دَخَلَتْ اُمَّةٌ لَّعَنَتْ اُخْتَهَا ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا ادَّارَكُوْا فِيْهَا جَمِيْعًا ۙ قَالَتْ اُخْرٰٮهُمْ لِاُوْلٰٮهُمْ رَبَّنَا هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ اَضَلُّوْنَا فَاٰتِهِمْ عَذَابًا ضِعْفًا مِّنَ النَّارِ  ؕ قَالَ لِكُلٍّ ضِعْفٌ وَّلٰكِنْ لَّا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(38)\nQAALA KHOLOO FEE OMAMIN QAD KHALAT MIN QABLEKUM MENAL JINNE WAL INSE FIL NAAR KULLAMAA DAKHALAT UMMATUN LLAA’ANAT AUKHTAHAA HATTAA EZAA ADDAARAKOOA FEEHAA JAMEE-A’A QAALAT AUKHRAAHUM LEAOOLAAHUM RABBANAA HAAOOLAAA-E AAZALLOONAA FA AATEHIM A’ZAABAN ZEA’FAN MENAL NAAR QAALA LEKULLIN ZEA’FUN LAAKIL LAA TA’LAMOON.\nHe will say: “Enter ye in the company of the peoples who passed away before you - men and jinns, - into the Fire.” Every time a new people enters, it curses its sister-people (that went before), until they follow each other, all into the Fire. Saith the last about the first: “Our Lord! it is these that misled us: so give them a double penalty in the Fire.” He will say: “Doubled for all” : but this ye do not understand. \nوَقَالَتْ اُوْلٰٮهُمْ لِاُخْرٰٮهُمْ فَمَا كَانَ لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ فَضْلٍ فَذُوْقُوا الْعَذَابَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(39)\nWA QAALAT AOOLAAHUM LEAUKHRAAHUM FAMAA KAANA LAKUM A’LAYNAA MIN FAZLIN FAZOOQOOA A’ZAABA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKSEBOONA.\nThen the first will say to the last: “See then! No advantage have ye over us; so taste ye of the penalty for all that ye did !” \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا عَنْهَا لَا تُفَتَّحُ لَهُمْ اَبْوَابُ السَّمَآءِ وَلَا يَدْخُلُوْنَ الْجَنَّةَ حَتّٰى يَلِجَ الْجَمَلُ فِىْ سَمِّ الْخِيَاطِ ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(40)\nINNAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WAASTAKBAROOA A’NHAA LAA TUFATTAHU LAHUM AABWAABU SAMAAA-E WA LAA YADKHOLOONA JANNATA HATTAA YALEJA AL-JAMALU FEE SAMME AL-KHEEATE WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL MUJREMEEN.\nTo those who reject Our signs and treat them with arrogance, no opening will there be of the gates of heaven, nor will they enter the garden, until the camel can pass through the eye of the needle: Such is Our reward for those in sin. \nلَهُمْ مِّنْ جَهَنَّمَ مِهَادٌ وَّمِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ غَوَاشٍ ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِى الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(41)\nLAHUM MIN JAHANNAMA MEHAADUN WA MIN FAWQEHIM GHAWAASHIN WA KAZAALEKA NAJZIL ZAALEMEEN.\nFor them there is Hell, as a couch (below) and folds and folds of covering above: such is Our requital of those who do wrong. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَاۤ  اُولٰۤئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِۚ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(42)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAA NUKALLEFU NAFSAN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA AOOLAAEKA ASHAABUN JANNAH HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nBut those who believe and work righteousness, no burden do We place on any soul, but that which it can bear, they will be Companions of the Garden, therein to dwell (for ever). \nوَنَزَعْنَا مَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِهِمْ مِّنْ غِلٍّ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهِمُ الْاَنْهٰرُۚ وَقَالُوا الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ هَدٰٮنَا لِهٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لِنَهْتَدِىَ لَوْلَاۤ اَنْ هَدٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ ۚ لَقَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُ رَبِّنَا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَنُوْدُوْۤا اَنْ تِلْكُمُ الْجَنَّةُ اُوْرِثْتُمُوْهَا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA NAZA’NAA MAA FEE SODOOREHIM MIN GHELLIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHEMU ANHAARO WA HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE HADAANAA LEHAAZAL WA MAA KUNNAA LENAHTADEAAA LAWLAA AN HADAANAA LAAHO LAQAD JAAA-AT RUSULU RABBENAA BIL-HAQQE WANOODOOA AN TELKUMU JANNATO AOORESTUMOOHAA BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd We shall remove from their hearts any lurking sense of injury;- beneath them will be rivers flowing;- and they shall say: “Praise be to Allah, who hath guided us to this (felicity): never could we have found guidance, had it not been for the guidance of Allah: indeed it was the truth, that the messengers of our Lord brought unto us.” And they shall hear the cry: “Behold! the garden before you! Ye have been made its inheritors, for your deeds (of righteousness).” \nوَنَادٰٓى اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِ اَصْحٰبَ النَّارِ اَنْ قَدْ وَجَدْنَا مَا وَعَدَنَا رَبُّنَا حَقًّا فَهَلْ وَجَدْتُّمْ مَّا وَعَدَ رَبُّكُمْ حَقًّا ؕ قَالُوْا نَعَمْ ۚ فَاَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌۢ بَيْنَهُمْ اَنْ لَّعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(44)\nWANAADAAA ASHAABUN JANNAH MASALAN NAAR AN QAD WAJADNAA MAA WA-A’DANAL RABBONAA HAQQAN FA HAL WAJADTTUM MAA WA-A’DAR RABBOKUM HAQQAN QAALOO NAA’AM FAAZZANA MUAZZENUN BAYNAHUM AN LLAA’NATU LAAHE A’LAL ZAALEMEEN.\nThe Companions of the Garden will call out to the Companions of the Fire: “We have indeed found the promises of our Lord to us true: Have you also found Your Lord's promises true?” They shall say, “Yes”; but a crier shall proclaim between them: “The curse of Allah is on the wrong-doers;- \nالَّذِيْنَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَيَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ۚ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ كٰفِرُوْنَۘ‏(45)\nLAZEENA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WAYABGHOONAHAA E’EWAJAN WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE KAAFEROON.\n“Those who would hinder (men) from the path of Allah and would seek in it something crooked: they were those who denied the Hereafter.” \nوَبَيْنَهُمَا حِجَابٌۚ وَعَلَى الْاَعْرَافِ رِجَالٌ يَّعْرِفُوْنَ كُلًّاۢ بِسِيْمٰٮهُمْ ۚ وَنَادَوْا اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ اَنْ سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ لَمْ يَدْخُلُوْهَا وَهُمْ يَطْمَعُوْنَ‏(46)\nWA BAYNAHOMAA HEJAABUN WA AL-AAA’RAAFE REJAALUN YYAA’REFOONA KULLAN BESEEMAAHUM WANAADAWA MASALAN JANNAH AN SALAAMUN A’LAYKUM LAM YADKHULOOHAA WA HUM YATMAU’OONA.\nBetween them shall be a veil, and on the heights will be men who would know every one by his marks: they will call out to the Companions of the Garden, “peace on you”: they will not have entered, but they will have an assurance (thereof). \nوَاِذَا صُرِفَتْ اَبْصَارُهُمْ تِلْقَآءَ اَصْحٰبِ النَّارِۙ قَالُوْا رَبَّنَا لَا تَجْعَلْنَا مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(47)\nWA EZAA SUREFAT AABSAARUHUM TILQAAA-A ASHAABIL NAAR QAALOO RABBANAA LAA TAJA’ALNAA LAAHA QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\n When their eyes shall be turned towards the Companions of the Fire, they will say: “Our Lord! send us not to the company of the wrong-doers.” \nوَنَادٰٓى اَصْحٰبُ الْاَعْرَافِ رِجَالًا يَّعْرِفُوْنَهُمْ بِسِيْمٰٮهُمْ قَالُوْا مَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْكُمْ جَمْعُكُمْ وَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ‏(48)\nWANAADAAA ASHAABUN AL-AAA’RAAFE REJAALAN YYAA’REFOONAHUM BESEEMAAHUM QAALOO MAA AGHNAA A’NKUM JAMU’UKUM WA MAA KUNTUM TASTAKBEROONA.\nThe men on the heights will call to certain men whom they will know from their marks, saying: “Of what profit to you were your hoards and your arrogant ways? \nاَهٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ الَّذِيْنَ اَقْسَمْتُمْ لَا يَنَالُهُمُ اللّٰهُ بِرَحْمَةٍ ؕ اُدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَنْتُمْ تَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(49)\nAAHAAAULAAE LAZEENA AAQSAMTUM LAA YANAALUHUMU LAAHO BERAHMATIN AUDKHULOOA JANNATA LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYKUM WA LAA ANTUM TAHZANOONA.\n“Behold! are these not the men whom you swore that Allah with His Mercy would never bless? Enter ye the Garden: no fear shall be on you, nor shall ye grieve.” \nوَنَادٰٓى اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ اَنْ اَفِيْضُوْا عَلَيْنَا مِنَ الْمَآءِ اَوْ مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ ؕ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ اللّٰهَ حَرَّمَهُمَا عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ ۙ‏(50)\nWANAADAAA ASHAABUN NAAR MASALAN JANNAH AN AFEEZOO A’LAYNAA MENAL AL-MAAE AW MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO QAALOO INNAL LAAHA HARRAMAHUMAA A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nThe Companions of the Fire will call to the Companions of the Garden: “Pour down to us water or anything that Allah doth provide for your sustenance.” They will say: “Both these things hath Allah forbidden to those who rejected Him.” \nالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا دِيْنَهُمْ لَهْوًا وَّلَعِبًا وَّغَرَّتْهُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا ۚ فَالْيَوْمَ نَنْسٰٮهُمْ كَمَا نَسُوْا لِقَآءَ يَوْمِهِمْ هٰذَا ۙ وَمَا كَانُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا يَجْحَدُوْنَ‏(51)\nLAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA DEENAHUM LAHWAN WWALAE’EBAN WWAGHARRATHUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA FALYAWMA NANSAAHUM KAMAA NASOOA LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEHEM HAAZAA WA MAA KAANOO BE-AAYAATENAA YAJHADOON.\n“Such as took their religion to be mere amusement and play, and were deceived by the life of the world.” That day shall We forget them as they forgot the meeting of this day of theirs, and as they were wont to reject Our signs. \nوَلَقَدْ جِئْنٰهُمْ بِكِتٰبٍ فَصَّلْنٰهُ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ هُدًى وَّرَحْمَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(52)\nWA LAQAD JENAAHUM BEKETAABIM FASSALNAAHU A’LAA I’LMIN HODAM WA RAHMATAL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nFor We had certainly sent unto them a Book, based on knowledge, which We explained in detail, a guide and a mercy to all who believe. \nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّا تَاْوِيْلَهٗؕ يَوْمَ يَاْتِىْ تَاْوِيْلُهٗ يَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ نَسُوْهُ مِنْ قَبْلُ قَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُ رَبِّنَا بِالْحَقِّۚ فَهَلْ لَّنَا مِنْ شُفَعَآءَ فَيَشْفَعُوْا لَنَاۤ اَوْ نُرَدُّ فَنَعْمَلَ غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ كُنَّا نَعْمَلُؕ قَدْ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(53)\nHAL YANZOROONA ILLAA TAAWEELAH YAWMA YAATEE TAAWEELUH YAQOOLO LAZEENA NASOOHU MIN QABLO QAD JAAA-AT RUSULU RABBENAA BIL-HAQQE FA HAL LANAA MIN SHUFAA’AAA FAYASHFAU’OOA LANAA AW NURADDU FANAA’MALA GHAYRA LAZEE KUNNAA NAA’MALU QAD KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nDo they just wait for the final fulfilment of the event? On the day the event is finally fulfilled, those who disregarded it before will say: “The messengers of our Lord did indeed bring true (tidings). Have we no intercessors now to intercede on our behalf? Or could we be sent back? then should we behave differently from our behaviour in the past.” In fact they will have lost their souls, and the things they invented will leave them in the lurch. \nاِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضَ فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ ثُمَّ اسْتَوٰى عَلَى الْعَرْشِ يُغْشِى الَّيْلَ النَّهَارَ يَطْلُبُهٗ حَثِيْثًا ۙ وَّالشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ وَالنُّجُوْمَ مُسَخَّرٰتٍۢ بِاَمْرِهٖ ؕ اَلَا لَهُ الْخَلْقُ وَالْاَمْرُ ؕ تَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(54)\nINNAL RABBAKOMUL LAAHO LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WA ARZA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN SUMMA TAWAA A’LAL A’RSHIL YUGHSHEAA LAYLA NAHAARA YATLUBUH HASEESAN WWAALSSHAMSA WAL QAMARA WAALNNUJOOMA MUSAKKHARAATIN LAAHO ALAA LAHUL AL-KHALQU AMRO TABAARAKAS-MO LAAHO RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nYour Guardian-Lord is Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth in six days, and is firmly established on the throne (of authority): He draweth the night as a veil o'er the day, each seeking the other in rapid succession: He created the sun, the moon, and the stars, (all) governed by laws under His command. Is it not His to create and to govern? Blessed be Allah, the Cherisher and Sustainer of the worlds! \nاُدْعُوْا رَبَّكُمْ تَضَرُّعًا وَّخُفْيَةً ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُعْتَدِيْنَ ۚ‏(55)\nAUDU’OOA TAQUL TAZARRUA’AN WWAKHUFYATAN INNAHU LAA YOHIBBUL MO’TADEEN.\nCall on your Lord with humility and in private: for Allah loveth not those who trespass beyond bounds. \nوَلَا تُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ بَعْدَ اِصْلَاحِهَا وَادْعُوْهُ خَوْفًا وَّطَمَعًا ؕ اِنَّ رَحْمَتَ اللّٰهِ قَرِيْبٌ مِّنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(56)\nWA LAA TUFSEDOO FIL ARZE BA’DA AESLAAHEHAA WAADU’OOHU BARQA KHAWFANW INNAL RAHMATAL LAAHE QAREEB MENAL MOHSENEEN.\nDo no mischief on the earth, after it hath been set in order, but call on Him with fear and longing (in your hearts): for the Mercy of Allah is (always) near to those who do good. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُرْسِلُ الرِّيٰحَ بُشْرًۢا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَقَلَّتْ سَحَابًا ثِقَالًا سُقْنٰهُ لِبَلَدٍ مَّيِّتٍ فَاَنْزَلْنَا بِهِ الْمَآءَ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖ مِنْ كُلِّ الثَّمَرٰتِؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُخْرِجُ الْمَوْتٰى لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(57)\nWA HOWA LAZEE YURSELUR REYAAHA BUSHRAM BAYNA YADAY FEE HATTAA EZAA AAQALLAT SAHAABAN SEQAALAN SUQNAAHU LEBALADIN MMAYTIN FA-ANZALNAA BEHIL MAAA-AH FA AKH-RAJNAA BEHI MIN KULLE AS-SAMARAATE KAZAALEKA NUKHREJU MAWTAA LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nIt is He Who sendeth the winds like heralds of glad tidings, going before His mercy: when they have carried the heavy-laden clouds, We drive them to a land that is dead, make rain to descend thereon, and produce every kind of harvest therewith: thus shall We raise up the dead: perchance ye may remember. \nوَالْبَلَدُ الطَّيِّبُ يَخْرُجُ نَبَاتُهٗ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهٖ ۚ وَالَّذِىْ خَبُثَ لَا يَخْرُجُ اِلَّا نَكِدًا ؕ كَذٰلِكَ نُصَرِّفُ الْاٰيٰتِ لِقَوْمٍ يَّشْكُرُوْنَ‏(58)\nWAL BALADU AT-TAYBU YAKHROJO NABAATUH BE-IZNIL RABBEHI WAL LAZEE KHABUSA LAA YAKHROJO ILLAA NAKEDAN KAZAALEKA NUSARREFU AAYAATE LE-QAWMIN-Y YYASHKUROONA.\nFrom the land that is clean and good, by the will of its Cherisher, springs up produce, (rich) after its kind: but from the land that is bad, springs up nothing but that which is niggardly: thus do we explain the signs by various (symbols) to those who are grateful. \nلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(59)\nLAQAD ARSALNAA ARSALNAA ELAA QAWMEHI FAQAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nWe sent Noah to his people. He said: “O my people! worship Allah! ye have no other god but Him. I fear for you the punishment of a dreadful day! \nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّا لَنَرٰٮكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(60)\nQAALA MALA-O MIN QAWMEHI INNAA LANARAAKA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nThe leaders of his people said: “Ah! we see thee evidently wandering (in mind).” \nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَيْسَ بِىْ ضَلٰلَةٌ وَّلٰكِنِّىْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(61)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI LAYSA BEE ZALAALATUN WWALAAKENNEAA RASOOLUM MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nHe said: “O my people! No wandering is there in my (mind): on the contrary I am a messenger from the Lord and Cherisher of the worlds! \nاُبَلِّغُكُمْ رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّىْ وَاَنْصَحُ لَكُمْ وَاَعْلَمُ مِنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(62)\nAUBALLEGHUKUM RESAALAATIL RABBEE WAANSAHU LAKUM WA A-A’LAMO MENAL LAAHE MAA LAA TA’LAMOON.\n“I but fulfil towards you the duties of my Lord's mission: Sincere is my advice to you, and I know from Allah something that ye know not. \nاَوَعَجِبْتُمْ اَنْ جَآءَكُمْ ذِكْرٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَلٰى رَجُلٍ مِّنْكُمْ لِيُنْذِرَكُمْ وَلِتَتَّقُوْا وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(63)\nAAWAA’AJEBTUM AN JAAA-AKUM ZIKRUNW MIN RABBEKUM A’LAA RAJULIN MINKUM LEENZERAKUM WALETATTAQOOA WA LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\n“Do ye wonder that there hath come to you a message from your Lord, through a man of your own people, to warn you, so that ye may fear Allah and haply receive His Mercy?” \nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَالَّذِيْنَ مَعَهٗ فِى الْفُلْكِ وَاَغْرَقْنَا الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا عَمِيْنَ‏(64)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-ANJAYNAAHO WAL LAZEENA MA-A’HU FIL FULKE WAAGHRAQNAA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN A’AMEENA.\nBut they rejected him, and We delivered him, and those with him, in the Ark: but We overwhelmed in the flood those who rejected Our signs. They were indeed a blind people! \nوَاِلٰى عَادٍ اَخَاهُمْ هُوْدًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(65)\nWA ELAA A’ADIN SAMOODA HOODAN QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH AFALAA TATTAQOON.\n To the 'Ad people, (We sent) Hud, one of their (own) brethren: He said: O my people! worship Allah! ye have no other god but Him will ye not fear (Allah)?” \nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّا لَنَرٰٮكَ فِىْ سَفَاهَةٍ وَّاِنَّا لَنَظُنُّكَ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(66)\nQAALA MALA-O LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI INNAA LANARAAKA FEE SAFAAHATIN WWAANNAA LANAZUNNUKA MENAL KAAZEBEEN.\nThe leaders of the Unbelievers among his people said: “Ah! we see thou art an imbecile!” and “We think thou art a liar!” \nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَيْسَ بِىْ سَفَاهَةٌ وَّلٰكِنِّىْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(67)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI LAYSA BEE SAFAAHATUN WWALAAKENNEAA RASOOLUM MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nHe said: “O my people! I am no imbecile, but (I am) a messenger from the Lord and Cherisher of the worlds! \nاُبَلِّغُكُمْ رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّىْ وَاَنَا لَكُمْ نَاصِحٌ اَمِيْنٌ‏(68)\nAUBALLEGHUKUM RESAALAATIL RABBEE ANAT LAKUM NAASEHUN AMEEN.\n“I but fulfil towards you the duties of my Lord's mission: I am to you a sincere and trustworthy adviser. \nاَوَعَجِبْتُمْ اَنْ جَآءَكُمْ ذِكْرٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَلٰى رَجُلٍ مِّنْكُمْ لِيُنْذِرَكُمْ ؕ وَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ ۚ خُلَفَآءَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ قَوْمِ نُوْحٍ وَّزَادَكُمْ فِى الْخَلْقِ بَصْۜطَةً فَاذْكُرُوْۤا اٰ لَۤاءَ اللّٰهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(69)\nAAWAA’AJEBTUM AN JAAA-AKUM ZIKRUNW MIN RABBEKUM A’LAA RAJULIN MINKUM LEENZERAKUM WA KOROO IZ JAA’ALAKUM KHULAFAAA MIN BA’DE QAWME NOOHIN WWAZAADAKUM FIL AL-KHALQE BASTATAN FA KOROO AAA LAAA LAAHE LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\n“Do ye wonder that there hath come to you a message from your Lord through a man of your own people, to warn you? call in remembrance that He made you inheritors after the people of Noah, and gave you a stature tall among the nations. Call in remembrance the benefits (ye have received) from Allah: that so ye may prosper.” \nقَالُوْۤا اَجِئْتَنَا لِنَعْبُدَ اللّٰهَ وَحْدَهٗ وَنَذَرَ مَا كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَا ۚ فَاْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(70)\nQAALOO AAJETANAA LENAA’BUDA LAAHA WAHDAH WANAZARA MAA KAANA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUNAA FAATENAA BEMAA TAE’EDUNAA IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nThey said: “Comest thou to us, that we may worship Allah alone, and give up the cult of our fathers? bring us what thou threatenest us with, if so be that thou tellest the truth!” \nقَالَ قَدْ وَقَعَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ رِجْسٌ وَّغَضَبٌؕ اَتُجَادِلُوْنَنِىْ فِىْۤ اَسْمَآءٍ سَمَّيْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَآؤُكُمْ مَّا نَزَّلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍؕ فَانْتَظِرُوْۤا اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُنْتَظِرِيْنَ‏(71)\nQAALA QAD WAQA-A’L A’LAYKUM MIN RABBEKUM REJSUN WWAGHAZABUN AATUJAADELOONANEAA FEE AASMAAIN SAMMAYTUMOOHAA ANTUM WAABAAUKUM MAA NAZZALAL LAAHO BEHAA MIN SULTAANIN FAANTAZEROOA INNEE MA-A’KUM MENAL AL-MUNTAZEREENA.\nHe said: “Punishment and wrath have already come upon you from your Lord: dispute ye with me over names which ye have devised - ye and your fathers, without authority from Allah? then wait: I am amongst you, also waiting.” \nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَالَّذِيْنَ مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَ قَطَعْنَا دَابِرَ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَمَا كَانُوْا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(72)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WAL LAZEENA MA-A’HU BERAHMATIN MINNAA WA QATAA’NAA DAABERA LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WA MAA KAANOO MUMENEENA.\nWe saved him and those who adhered to him. By Our mercy, and We cut off the roots of those who rejected Our signs and did not believe. \nوَاِلٰى ثَمُوْدَ اَخَاهُمْ صٰلِحًا ۘ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوْا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ قَدْ جَآءَتْكُمْ بَيِّنَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ ؕ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةُ اللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اٰيَةً فَذَرُوْهَا تَاْكُلْ فِىْۤ اَرْضِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(73)\nWA ELAA ELAA SAMOODA AKHAAHUM QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODOO LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH QAD JAAA-ATKUM BAYNATUN MIN RABBEKUM HAAZEHI NAAQATU LAAHE LAKUM AAYATAL FAZAROOHAA TAAKUL FEE AARZE LAAHE WA LAA TAMASSOOHAA BE-SOOO-IN FAYAAKHUZAKUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nTo the Thamud people (We sent) Salih, one of their own brethren: He said: “O my people! worship Allah: ye have no other god but Him. Now hath come unto you a clear (Sign) from your Lord! This she-camel of Allah is a Sign unto you: So leave her to graze in Allah's earth, and let her come to no harm, or ye shall be seized with a grievous punishment. \nوَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ جَعَلَكُمْ خُلَفَآءَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ عَادٍ وَّبَوَّاَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ تَتَّخِذُوْنَ مِنْ سُهُوْلِهَا قُصُوْرًا وَّتَنْحِتُوْنَ الْجِبَالَ بُيُوْتًا ۚ فَاذْكُرُوْۤا اٰ لَۤاءَ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(74)\nWA KOROO IZ JAA’ALAKUM KHULAFAAA MIN BA’DE A’ADIN WWABAWAAKUM FIL ARZE TATTAKHEZOONA MIN SUHOOLEHAA QUSOORAN WWATANHETOONA JEBAALA BUYOOTAN FA KOROO AAA LAAA LAAHE WA LAA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\n“And remember how He made you inheritors after the 'Ad people and gave you habitations in the land: ye build for yourselves palaces and castles in (open) plains, and carve out homes in the mountains; so bring to remembrance the benefits (ye have received) from Allah, and refrain from evil and mischief on the earth.” \nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا لِمَنْ اٰمَنَ مِنْهُمْ اَتَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّ صٰلِحًا مُّرْسَلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖؕ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلَ بِهٖ مُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(75)\nQAALA MALA-O LAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA MIN QAWMEHI LILLAZEENA TUZ-E’FOO LEMAN-Y AAMANA MINHUM AATAA’LAMOONA ANNAL AKHAAHUM MMURSALUN MIN RABBEH QAALOO INNAA BEMAA AURSELA BEHI MOAMENOON.\nThe leaders of the arrogant party among his people said to those who were reckoned powerless - those among them who believed: “know ye indeed that Salih is a messenger from his Lord?” They said: “We do indeed believe in the revelation which hath been sent through him.” \nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْۤا اِنَّا بِالَّذِىْۤ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِهٖ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(76)\nQAALA LAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA INNAA BIL-LAZEE AAMANTUM BEHI KAAFEROON.\nThe Arrogant party said: “For our part, we reject what ye believe in.” \nفَعَقَرُوا النَّاقَةَ وَعَتَوْا عَنْ اَمْرِ رَبِّهِمْ وَ قَالُوْا يٰصٰلِحُ ائْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ‏(77)\nFAA’AQAROOA AN-NAAQATA WAA’ATAWA A’N AMRE RABBEHIM WA QAALOO YAASAALEHU E-ATENAA BEMAA TAE’EDUNAA IN KUNTA MENAL MURSALEEN.\nThen they ham-strung the she-camel, and insolently defied the order of their Lord, saying: “O Salih! bring about thy threats, if thou art a messenger (of Allah)!” \nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَ‏(78)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUR RAJFATO FA-ASBAHOO FEE DAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nSo the earthquake took them unawares, and they lay prostrate in their homes in the morning! \nفَتَوَلّٰى عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَقَدْ اَبْلَغْتُكُمْ رِسَالَةَ رَبِّىْ وَنَصَحْتُ لَكُمْ وَلٰكِنْ لَّا تُحِبُّوْنَ النّٰصِحِيْنَ‏(79)\nFA TAWALLAA A’NHUM WA QAALA LE-QAWMEHI LAQAD AABLAGHTUKUM RESAALATA RABBEE WANASAHTU LAKUM WA LAAKIL LAA TUHEBBOONA NAASEHEEN.\nSo Salih left them, saying: “O my people! I did indeed convey to you the message for which I was sent by my Lord: I gave you good counsel, but ye love not good counsellors!” \nوَلُوْطًا اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اَتَاْتُوْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ مَا سَبَقَكُمْ بِهَا مِنْ اَحَدٍ مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(80)\nWA LOOTAN IZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI ATAATOONAL FAAHESHATA MAA SABAQAKUM BEHAA MIN AHADIM MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nWe also (sent) Lut: He said to his people: “Do ye commit lewdness such as no people in creation (ever) committed before you? \nاِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الرِّجَالَ شَهْوَةً مِّنْ دُوْنِ النِّسَآءِ ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ مُّسْرِفُوْنَ‏(81)\nINNAKUM LATAATOO NAR REJAALA SHAHWATAM MIN DOONIL NESAAA-E BAL ANTUM QAWMUN MMUSREFOONA.\n“For ye practise your lusts on men in preference to women : ye are indeed a people transgressing beyond bounds.” \nوَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوْۤا اَخْرِجُوْهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْيَتِكُمْ ۚ اِنَّهُمْ اُنَاسٌ يَّتَطَهَّرُوْنَ‏(82)\nWA MAA KAANA JAWAABA QAWMEHI ILLAA AN QAALOO AAKHREJOOHUM MIN QARYATEKUM INNAHUM ONAASUYN YATATAHHAROON.\nAnd his people gave no answer but this: they said, “Drive them out of your city: these are indeed men who want to be clean and pure!” \nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ ۖ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(83)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO AHLAHU ILLAA RA-ATAHU KAANAT MENAL GHAABEREEN.\nBut we saved him and his family, except his wife: she was of those who legged behind. \nوَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَّطَرًا ؕ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(84)\n58 WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHIM MATARAA FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUJREMEEN.\nAnd we rained down on them a shower (of brimstone): Then see what was the end of those who indulged in sin and crime! \nوَاِلٰى مَدْيَنَ اَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ قَدْ جَآءَتْكُمْ بَيِّنَةٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ بَعْدَ اِصْلَاحِهَا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ ۚ‏(85)\nWA ELAA MADYANA SAMOODA SHO-A’YBAA QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH QAD JAAA-ATKUM BAYNATUN MIN RABBEKUM FAAWFOOA AL-KAYLA WA MEEZAAN WA LAA TABKHASOOA NAASA AASHYAAAHUM WA LAA TUFSEDOO FIL ARZE BA’DA AESLAAHEHAA ZAA ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nTo the Madyan people We sent Shu'aib, one of their own brethren: he said: “O my people! worship Allah; Ye have no other god but Him. Now hath come unto you a clear (Sign) from your Lord! Give just measure and weight, nor withhold from the people the things that are their due; and do no mischief on the earth after it has been set in order: that will be best for you, if ye have Faith. \nوَلَا تَقْعُدُوْا بِكُلِّ صِرَاطٍ تُوْعِدُوْنَ وَتَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ مَنْ اٰمَنَ بِهٖ وَتَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ۚ وَاذْكُرُوْۤا اِذْ كُنْتُمْ قَلِيْلًا فَكَثَّرَكُمْوَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(86)\nWA LAA TAQU’UDOOA BEKULLE SERAATIM TOOE’EDOONA WATASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE MAN AAMANA BEHI WATABGHOONAHAA E’EWAJAN WA KOROO IZ KUNTUM QALEELAA FAKASSARAKUMWAANZUROOA KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUFSEDEEN.\n“And squat not on every road, breathing threats, hindering from the path of Allah those who believe in Him, and seeking in it something crooked; But remember how ye were little, and He gave you increase. And hold in your mind's eye what was the end of those who did mischief. \nوَاِنْ كَانَ طَآئِفَةٌ مِّنْكُمْ اٰمَنُوْا بِالَّذِىْۤ اُرْسِلْتُ بِهٖ وَطَآئِفَةٌ لَّمْ يُؤْمِنُوْا فَاصْبِرُوْا حَتّٰى يَحْكُمَ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَنَا ۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(87)\nWA KAANA TAAEFATUN MINKUM AAMANOO BIL-LAZEE AURSELTU BEHI WA TAAA-EFATUM LAM YOAMENOO FAASBEROOA HATTAA YAHKUMA LAAHO BAYNANAA WA HOWA KHAYRUR HAAKEMEEN.\n“And if there is a party among you who believes in the message with which I have been sent, and a party which does not believe, hold yourselves in patience until Allah doth decide between us: for He is the best to decide. \nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ لَنُخْرِجَنَّكَ يٰشُعَيْبُ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَكَ مِنْ قَرْيَتِنَاۤ اَوْ لَتَعُوْدُنَّ فِىْ مِلَّتِنَا ؕ قَالَ اَوَلَوْ كُنَّا كَارِهِيْنَ ۚ‏(88)\nQAALA MALA-O LAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA MIN QAWMEHI LANUKHREJANNAKA YAASHUA’AYBU WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’KA MIN QARYATENAA AW LATAU’OODUNNA FEE MELLATENAA QAALA LAW KUNNAA KAAREHEENA.\n(9)  The leaders, the arrogant party among his people, said: “O Shu'aib! we shall certainly drive thee out of our city - (thee) and those who believe with thee; or else ye (thou and they) shall have to return to our ways and religion.” He said: “What! even though we do detest (them)? \nقَدِ افْتَرَيْنَا عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اِنْ عُدْنَا فِىْ مِلَّتِكُمْ بَعْدَ اِذْ نَجّٰٮنَا اللّٰهُ مِنْهَا ؕ وَمَا يَكُوْنُ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّعُوْدَ فِيْهَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّنَا ؕ وَسِعَ رَبُّنَا كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًاؕ عَلَى اللّٰهِ تَوَكَّلْنَا ؕ رَبَّنَا افْتَحْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَ قَوْمِنَا بِالْحَقِّ وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْفٰتِحِيْنَ‏(89)\nQADE AFTARAYNAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN IN U’UDNAA FEE MELLATEKUM BA’DA IZ NAJJAANAA LAAHO MINHAA WA MAA LAHUL LANAA AN NNAU’OODA FEEHAA ILLAA AN YASHAAA-AL LAAHO RABBONAA WASEA’ RABBONAA KULLA SHAY-IN E’ELMAN A’LAL LAAHE TAWAKKALNAA RABBANAA AFTAH BAYNANAA WA BAYNA QAWMENAA BIL-HAQQE WA ANTA KHAYRUR AL-FAATEHEENA.\n“We should indeed invent a lie against Allah, if we returned to your ways after Allah hath rescued us therefrom; nor could we by any manner of means return thereto unless it be as in the will and plan of Allah, Our Lord. Our Lord can reach out to the utmost recesses of things by His knowledge. In the Allah is our trust. our Lord! decide Thou between us and our people in truth, for Thou art the best to decide.” \nوَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ لَئِنِ اتَّبَعْتُمْ شُعَيْبًا اِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(90)\nWA QAALA MALA-O LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI LAENE ATTABAA’TUM SHO-A’YBAA INNAKUM EZAL LLAKHAASEROONA.\nThe leaders, the unbelievers among his people, said: “If ye follow Shu'aib, be sure then ye are ruined!” \nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَ ۛۙ  ۚ   ۖ‏(91)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUR RAJFATO FA-ASBAHOO FEE DAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nBut the earthquake took them unawares, and they lay prostrate in their homes before the morning! \nالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا شُعَيْبًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ۛۚ اَ لَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا شُعَيْبًا كَانُوْا هُمُ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(92)\nLAZEENA KAZZABOO SHO-A’YBAA KA-AN LAM YAGHNAWA FEEHAA LAZEENA KAZZABOO SHO-A’YBAA KAANOO HOMUL KHAASEREEN.\nThe men who reject Shu'aib became as if they had never been in the homes where they had flourished: the men who rejected Shu'aib - it was they who were ruined! \nفَتَوَلّٰى عَنْهُمْ وَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ لَقَدْ اَبْلَغْتُكُمْ رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّىْ وَنَصَحْتُ لَكُمْۚ فَكَيْفَ اٰسٰی عَلٰى قَوْمٍ كٰفِرِيْنَ‏(93)\nFA TAWALLAA A’NHUM WA QAALA LE-QAWMEHI LAQAD AABLAGHTUKUM RESAALAATIL RABBEE WANASAHTU LAKUM FA-KAYFA AAASAAY A’LAA QAWMIN KAAFEREEN.\nSo Shu'aib left them, saying: “O my people! I did indeed convey to you the messages for which I was sent by my Lord: I gave you good counsel, but how shall I lament over a people who refuse to believe!” \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا فِىْ قَرْيَةٍ مِّنْ نَّبِىٍّ اِلَّاۤ اَخَذْنَاۤ اَهْلَهَا بِالْبَاْسَآءِ وَالضَّرَّآءِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَضَّرَّعُوْنَ‏(94)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA FEE QARYATINW MIN NNABEAAAIN ILLAA AKHAZNAA JA-A’LA BE-BAA-SAAA-E WAZ ZARRAAA-E LA-A’LLAHUM YAZZARRAU’OONA.\nWhenever We sent a prophet to a town, We took up its people in suffering and adversity, in order that they might learn humility. \nثُمَّ بَدَّلْنَا مَكَانَ السَّيِّئَةِ الْحَسَنَةَ حَتّٰى عَفَوْا وَّقَالُوْا قَدْ مَسَّ اٰبَآءَنَا الضَّرَّآءُ وَالسَّرَّآءُ فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(95)\nSUMMA BAD-DALNAA MAKAANA AS-SAYATE AL-HASANATA HATTAA A’AFAWA WA QAALOO QAD MASSAN AABAAA-ANAA AZ-ZARRAAU WAALSSARRAAU FAAKHAZNAAHUM BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThen We changed their suffering into prosperity, until they grew and multiplied, and began to say: “Our fathers (too) were touched by suffering and affluence” ... Behold! We called them to account of a sudden, while they realised not (their peril). \nوَلَوْ اَنَّ اَهْلَ الْقُرٰٓى اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّقَوْا لَفَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَرَكٰتٍ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَلٰكِنْ كَذَّبُوْا فَاَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(96)\nWA LAW ANNAL AHLAL QORAA AAMANOO AAMANOO LAFATAHNAA A’LAYHIM BARAKAATIN MENAL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE WA LAAKIL KAZZABOO FAAKHAZNAAHUM BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nIf the people of the towns had but believed and feared Allah, We should indeed have opened out to them (All kinds of) blessings from heaven and earth; but they rejected (the truth), and We brought them to book for their misdeeds. \nاَفَاَمِنَ اَهْلُ الْقُرٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتِيَهُمْ بَاْسُنَا بَيَاتًا وَّهُمْ نَآئِمُوْنَؕ‏(97)\nAAFAAMENA AAHLU QORAA AN YYAATEEHUM BAASUNAA BAYAATAN WA HUM NAAEMOONA.\nDid the people of the towns feel secure against the coming of Our wrath by night while they were asleep? \nاَوَاَمِنَ اَهْلُ الْقُرٰٓى اَنْ يَّاْتِيَهُمْ بَاْسُنَا ضُحًى وَّهُمْ يَلْعَبُوْنَ‏(98)\nAAWAAMENA AAHLU QORAA AN YYAATEEHUM BAASUNAA ZUHAN WA HUM YALA’ABOONA.\nOr else did they feel secure against its coming in broad daylight while they played about (care-free)? \nاَفَاَمِنُوْا مَكْرَ اللّٰهِ ۚ فَلَا يَاْمَنُ مَكْرَ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْقَوْمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(99)\nAAFAAMENOOA MAKRA LAAHE FALAA YAAMANU MAKRA LAAHE ILLAA AL-QAWMU KHAASEROON.\nDid they then feel secure against the plan of Allah? but no one can feel secure from the Plan of Allah, except those (doomed) to ruin! \nاَوَلَمْ يَهْدِ لِلَّذِيْنَ يَرِثُوْنَ الْاَرْضَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اَهْلِهَاۤ اَنْ لَّوْ نَشَآءُ اَصَبْنٰهُمْ بِذُنُوْبِهِمْ ۚ وَنَطْبَعُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوْنَ‏(100)\nAWALAM YAHDE LILLAZEENA YARESOONA ARZA MIN BA’DE AHLEHAA AN LAW NASHAAA-O AASABNAAHUM BEZUNOOBEHEM WANATBAU’U A’LAA QOLOOBEHIM FAHUM LAA YAS-MA-O’ONA.\nTo those who inherit the earth in succession to its (previous) possessors, is it not a guiding, (lesson) that, if We so willed, We could punish them (too) for their sins, and seal up their hearts so that they could not hear? \nتِلْكَ الْقُرٰى نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآئِهَا ۚ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ ۚ فَمَا كَانُوْا لِيُؤْمِنُوْا بِمَا كَذَّبُوْا مِنْ قَبْلُ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يَطْبَعُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى قُلُوْبِ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(101)\nTILKA KORAA NAQUSSU A’LAYKA MIN AANBAAEHAA WA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM JAAA-ATHUM BIL-BAYYENAATE FAMAA KAANOO LE-YOAMENOO BEMAA KAZZABOO MIN QABLO KAZAALEKA YATBA-U’L LAAHO A’LAA QOLOOBIL KAAFEREEN.\nSuch were the towns whose story We (thus) relate unto thee: There came indeed to them their messengers with clear (signs): But they would not believe what they had rejected before. Thus doth Allah seal up the hearts of those who reject faith. \nوَمَا وَجَدْنَا لِاَكْثَرِهِمْ مِّنْ عَهْدٍۚ وَاِنْ وَّجَدْنَاۤ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(102)\nWA MAA WAJADNAA LE-AKSAREHIM MIN A’AHDIN WA WWAJADNAA AKSARAHUM LAFAASEQEENA.\nMost of them We found not men (true) to their covenant: but most of them We found rebellious and disobedient. \nثُمَّ بَعَثْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ مُّوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ئِهٖ فَظَلَمُوْا بِهَا ۚ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(103)\nSUMMA BAA’ASNAA MIN BA’DEHIM MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA ELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAAEH FA ZALAMOO BEHAA FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MUFSEDEEN.\nThen after them We sent Moses with Our signs to Pharaoh and his chiefs, but they wrongfully rejected them: So see what was the end of those who made mischief. \nوَ قَالَ مُوْسٰى يٰفِرْعَوْنُ اِنِّىْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(104)\nWA QAALA MOOSAA YAA FIRA’WNO INNEE RASOOLUM MIN RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nMoses said: “O Pharaoh! I am a messenger from the Lord of the worlds, \nحَقِيْقٌ عَلٰٓى اَنْ لَّاۤ اَقُوْلَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْحَقَّ ؕ قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِبَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاَرْسِلْ مَعِىَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ؕ‏(105)\nHAQEEQUN A’LAA AN LAA AAQOOLA A’LAL LAAHE ILLAA HAQQA QAD JETUKUM BE-BAYYENAH MIN RABBEKUM FAARSEL MA-E’YA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nOne for whom it is right to say nothing but truth about Allah. Now have I come unto you (people), from your Lord, with a clear (Sign): So let the Children of Israel depart along with me.” \nقَالَ اِنْ كُنْتَ جِئْتَ بِاٰيَةٍ فَاْتِ بِهَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(106)\nQAALA IN KUNTA BIL-HAQ BE-AAYATIL FAATE BEHAA IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\n(Pharaoh) said: “If indeed thou hast come with a Sign, show it forth, if thou tellest the truth.” \nفَاَلْقٰى عَصَاهُ فَاِذَا هِىَ ثُعْبَانٌ مُّبِيْنٌ  ۖ ۚ‏(107)\nFAALQAA A’ASAAHU FA-EZAA HEYA SUA’BAANUN MOBEEN.\nThen (Moses) threw his rod, and behold! it was a serpent, plain (for all to see)! \nوَّنَزَعَ يَدَهٗ فَاِذَا هِىَ بَيْضَآءُ لِلنّٰظِرِيْنَ‏(108)\nWWANAZAA’A YADAH FA-EZAA HEYA BAYZAAU LELNNAAZEREENA.\nAnd he drew out his hand, and behold! it was white to all beholders! \nقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِ فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَسٰحِرٌ عَلِيْمٌ ۙ‏(109)\nQAALA MALA-O MIN QAWME FIR-A’WNA INNAL HAAZAA LASAAHERUN A’LEEM.\nSaid the Chiefs of the people of Pharaoh: “This is indeed a sorcerer well-versed. \nيُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّخْرِجَكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ ۚ فَمَاذَا تَاْمُرُوْنَ‏(110)\nYYUREEDU AN YYUKHREJAKUM MIN AARZEKUM FA MAA TAAMUROONA.\n“His plan is to get you out of your land: then what is it ye counsel?” \nقَالُوْآ اَرْجِهْ وَاَخَاہُ وَاَرْسِلْ فِی الْمَدَآئِنِ حٰشِرِیْنَ ۙ‏(111)\nBA’ZIN AARJEH WAAKHAAHU WAARSEL FEE AL-MADAAENE HAASHEREENA.\nThey said: “Keep him and his brother in suspense (for a while); and send to the cities men to collect- \nيَاْتُوْكَ بِكُلِّ سٰحِرٍ عَلِيْمٍ‏(112)\nYAATOOKA BEKULLE SAAHERIN A’LEEM.\nAnd bring up to thee all (our) sorcerers well-versed.” \nوَجَآءَ السَّحَرَةُ فِرْعَوْنَ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّ لَنَا لَاَجْرًا اِنْ كُنَّا نَحْنُ الْغٰلِبِيْنَ‏(113)\nWA JAAA-A AS-SAHARATU FIR-A’WNA QAALOO INNAL LANAA LAAJRAN IN KUNNAA NAHNO AL-GHAALEBEENA.\nSo there came the sorcerers to Pharaoh: They said, “of course we shall have a (suitable) reward if we win!” \nقَالَ نَعَمْ وَاِنَّكُمْ لَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ‏(114)\nQAALA NAA’AM WA INNAKUM LAMENAS MOQARRABEEN.\nHe said: “Yea, (and more), for ye shall in that case be (raised to posts) nearest (to my person).” \nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِمَّاۤ اَنْ تُلْقِىَ وَاِمَّاۤ اَنْ نَّكُوْنَ نَحْنُ الْمُلْقِيْنَ‏(115)\nQAALOO MOOSAA IMMAA AN TULQEAAA WA AMMAA AN NNAKOONA NAHNO AL-MULQEENA.\nThey said: “O Moses! wilt thou throw (first), or shall we have the (first) throw?” \nقَالَ اَلْقُوْا ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَلْقَوْا سَحَرُوْۤا اَعْيُنَ النَّاسِ وَاسْتَرْهَبُوْهُمْ وَجَآءُوْ بِسِحْرٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(116)\nQAALA AALQOOA FALAMMAA AALQAWA SAHAROOA AAA’YUNA NAASE WAASTARHABOOHUM WA JAAA-OO BESEHRIN A’ZEEM.\nSaid Moses: “Throw ye (first).” So when they threw, they bewitched the eyes of the people, and struck terror into them: for they showed a great (feat of) magic. \nوَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اَنْ اَلْقِ عَصَاكَ ۚ فَاِذَا هِىَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَاْفِكُوْنَ ۚ‏(117)\nWA AWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA AN AALQE A’SAAKA FA-EZAA HEYA TALQAFU MAA YAAFEKOONA.\n We put it into Moses's mind by inspiration: “Throw (now) thy rod”:and behold! it swallows up straight away all the falsehoods which they fake! \nفَوَقَعَ الْحَقُّ وَبَطَلَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَۚ‏(118)\nFA WAQA-A’L HAQQO WABATALA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThus truth was confirmed, and all that they did was made of no effect. \nفَغُلِبُوْا هُنَالِكَ وَانْقَلَبُوْا صٰغِرِيْنَۚ‏(119)\nFAGHULEBOOA HONAALEKAB WA QALABOO SAAGHEREENA.\nSo the (great ones) were vanquished there and then, and were made to look small. \nوَ اُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سٰجِدِيْنَ ۙ‏(120)\nWA ULQEYA AS-SAHARATU SAAJEDEENA.\nBut the sorcerers fell down prostrate in adoration. \nقَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ ۙ‏(121)\nQAALOO AAMANNAA BE RABBIL A’ALAMEEN.\nSaying: “We believe in the Lord of the Worlds, \nرَبِّ مُوْسٰى وَهٰرُوْنَ‏(122)\nRABBE MOOSAA WA AALO.\n“The Lord of Moses and Aaron.” \nقَالَ فِرْعَوْنُ اٰمَنْتُمْ بِهٖ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْۚ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَمَكْرٌ مَّكَرْتُمُوْهُ فِى الْمَدِيْنَةِ لِتُخْرِجُوْا مِنْهَاۤ اَهْلَهَا ۚ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(123)\nQAALA FIRA’WNO AAMANTUM BEHI QABLA AN AAAZANA LAKUM INNAL HAAZAA LAMAKRUN MMAKARTUMOOHU FIL MADEENATE LETUKHREJOOA MINHAA JA-A’LA FA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON.\nSaid Pharaoh: “Believe ye in Him before I give you permission? Surely this is a trick which ye have planned in the city to drive out its people: but soon shall ye know (the consequences). \nلَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ ثُمَّ لَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(124)\nLAAQATTEA’ANNA AAYDEEKUM WAARJULAKUM MIN KHELAAFIN SUMMA LAASALLEBANNAKUM AJMA-E’ENA.\n“Be sure I will cut off your hands and your feet on apposite sides, and I will cause you all to die on the cross.” \nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اِلٰى رَبِّنَا مُنْقَلِبُوْنَۚ‏(125)\nQAALOO INNAA ELAA RABBENAA MUNQALEBOONA.\nThey said: “For us, We are but sent back unto our Lord: \nوَمَا تَنْقِمُ مِنَّاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ اٰمَنَّا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّنَا لَمَّا جَآءَتْنَا ؕ رَبَّنَاۤ اَفْرِغْ عَلَيْنَا صَبْرًا وَّتَوَفَّنَا مُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(126)\nWA MAA TANQEMU MINNAA ILLAA AN AAMANNAA BE-AAYAATIL RABBENAA LAMMAA JAAATNAA RABBANAA AFRIGH A’LAYNAA SABRANW WWATAWAFFANAA MUSLEMEEN.\n“But thou dost wreak thy vengeance on us simply because we believed in the Signs of our Lord when they reached us! Our Lord! pour out on us patience and constancy, and take our souls unto thee as Muslims (who bow to thy will)! \nوَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِ فِرْعَوْنَ اَتَذَرُ مُوْسٰى وَقَوْمَهٗ لِيُفْسِدُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَيَذَرَكَ وَاٰلِهَتَكَ ؕ قَالَ سَنُقَتِّلُ اَبْنَآءَهُمْ وَنَسْتَحْىٖ نِسَآءَهُمْ ۚ وَاِنَّا فَوْقَهُمْ قَاهِرُوْنَ‏(127)\nWA QAALA MALA-O MIN QAWME FIR-A’WNA AATAZARU MOOSAA WAQAWMAH LEEFSEDOOA FIL ARZE WAYAZARAKA WAALEHATAKA QAALA SANUQATTELU YOZABBEHO WANASTAHAA WA YASTAHYEE WA INNAA FAWQAHUM QAAHEROONA.\nSaid the chiefs of Pharaoh's people: “Wilt thou leave Moses and his people, to spread mischief in the land, and to abandon thee and thy gods?” He said: “Their male children will we slay; (only) their females will we save alive; and we have over them (power) irresistible.” \nقَالَ مُوْسٰى لِقَوْمِهِ اسْتَعِيْنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَاصْبِرُوْا ۚ اِنَّ الْاَرْضَ لِلّٰهِ ۙ يُوْرِثُهَا مَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ ؕ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(128)\nQAALA MOOSAA LEQAWMEHE AAMANUS BIL-LAAHE WAASBEROOA INNAL ARZA LILLAAHE YOORESUHAA MAN YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI A-A’QEBATO LILMUTTAQEEN.\nSaid Moses to his people: “Pray for help from Allah, and (wait) in patience and constancy: for the earth is Allah's, to give as a heritage to such of His servants as He pleaseth; and the end is (best) for the righteous. \nقَالُوْۤا اُوْذِيْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ تَاْتِيَنَا وَمِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جِئْتَنَا ؕ قَالَ عَسٰى رَبُّكُمْ اَنْ يُّهْلِكَ عَدُوَّكُمْ وَيَسْتَخْلِفَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ فَيَنْظُرَ كَيْفَ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(129)\nQAALOO AOOZEENAA MIN QABLE AN TAATEENAA WA MIN BA’DE MAA JETANAA QAALA A’SAA RABBOKUM AN YYUHLEKA A’ADOOKUM WAYASTAKHLEFAKUM FIL ARZE FAYANZURA KAYFA TA’MALOON.\nThey said: “We have had (nothing but) trouble, both before and after thou camest to us.” He said: “It may be that your Lord will destroy your enemy and make you inheritors in the earth; that so He may try you by your deeds.” \nوَلَقَدْ اَخَذْنَاۤ اٰلَ فِرْعَوْنَ بِالسِّنِيْنَ وَنَقْصٍ مِّنَ الثَّمَرٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَذَّكَّرُوْنَ‏(130)\nWA LAQAD AKHAZNAA AALA FIR-A’WNA BEALSSENEENA WA NAQSIM MENAL SAMARAATE LA-A’LLAHUM YAZZAKKAROONA.\nWe punished the people of Pharaoh with years (of droughts) and shortness of crops; that they might receive admonition. \nفَاِذَا جَآءَتْهُمُ الْحَسَنَةُ قَالُوْا لَنَا هٰذِهٖ ۚ وَاِنْ تُصِبْهُمْ سَيِّئَةٌ يَّطَّيَّرُوْا بِمُوْسٰى وَمَنْ مَّعَهٗ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّمَا طٰٓئِرُهُمْ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(131)\nFA-EZAA JAAA-ATHOMUL TASTAWIL QAALOO LANAA HAAZEHI WA IN TOSIBHUM SAYYE-ATUM YYATTAYROOA BE-MOOSAA WA MAN MMAA’AH ALAA INNAMAA TAAAERUHUM I’NDAL LAAHE LAAKINNAL AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nBut when good (times) came, they said, “This is due to us;” When gripped by calamity, they ascribed it to evil omens connected with Moses and those with him! Behold! in truth the omens of evil are theirs in Allah's sight, but most of them do not understand! \nوَقَالُوْا مَهْمَا تَاْتِنَا بِهٖ مِنْ اٰيَةٍ لِّتَسْحَرَنَا بِهَا ۙ فَمَا نَحْنُ لَكَ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(132)\nWA QAALOO MAHMAA TAATENAA BEHI MIN AAYATIM LLETASHARANAA BEHAA FAMAA NAHNO LAKA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nThey said (to Moses): “Whatever be the Signs thou bringest, to work therewith thy sorcery on us, we shall never believe in thee. \nفَاَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الطُّوْفَانَ وَالْجَرَادَ وَالْقُمَّلَ وَالضَّفَادِعَ وَالدَّمَ اٰيٰتٍ مُّفَصَّلٰتٍ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(133)\nFA-ARSALNAA A’LAYHEMUL AT-TOOFAANA WAL JARAADA WAL QUMMALA WAALZZAFAADEA’A WAD DAMA AAYAATIM MMUFASSALAATIN FAS-TAKBAROO WA KAANOO QAWMAN MMUJREMEENA.\nSo We sent (plagues) on them: Wholesale death, Locusts, Lice, Frogs, And Blood: Signs openly self-explained: but they were steeped in arrogance, a people given to sin. \nوَلَمَّا وَقَعَ عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّجْزُ قَالُوْا يٰمُوْسَى ادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ بِمَا عَهِدَ عِنْدَكَۚ لَئِنْ كَشَفْتَ عَنَّا الرِّجْزَ لَنُؤْمِنَنَّ لَكَ وَلَنُرْسِلَنَّ مَعَكَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَۚ‏(134)\nWA LAMMAA WAQA-A’L A’LAYHEMUL AR-REJZU QAALOO YAA MOOSAL O’ LANAA RABBAKA BEMAA A’AHEDA E’ENDAKA LAIL KASHAFTA WAGH AR-REJZA LANUMENANNA LAKA WALANURSELANNA MA-A’KA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ.\nEvery time the penalty fell on them, they said: “O Moses! on your behalf call on thy Lord in virtue of his promise to thee: If thou wilt remove the penalty from us, we shall truly believe in thee, and we shall send away the Children of Israel with thee.” \nفَلَمَّا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمُ الرِّجْزَ اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ هُمْ بٰلِغُوْهُ اِذَا هُمْ يَنْكُثُوْنَ‏(135)\nFALAMMAA KASHAFNAA A’NHOMUL AR-REJZA ELAA ELAA HUM BAALEGHOOHU EZAA HUM YANKUSOONA.\nBut every time We removed the penalty from them according to a fixed term which they had to fulfil, Behold! they broke their word! \nفَانْتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ فِى الْيَمِّ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَكَانُوْا عَنْهَا غٰفِلِيْنَ‏(136)\nFAN-TAQAMNAA MINHUM FAAGHRAQNAAHUM FIL WA BE-ANNAHUM KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WA KAANOO A’NHAA GHAAFELEENA.\nSo We exacted retribution from them: We drowned them in the sea, because they rejected Our Signs and failed to take warning from them. \nوَاَوْرَثْنَا الْقَوْمَ الَّذِيْنَ كَانُوْا يُسْتَضْعَفُوْنَ مَشَارِقَ الْاَرْضِ وَمَغَارِبَهَا الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا ؕ وَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ الْحُسْنٰى عَلٰى بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَۙ بِمَا صَبَرُوْا ؕ وَدَمَّرْنَا مَا كَانَ يَصْنَعُ فِرْعَوْنُ وَقَوْمُهٗ وَمَا كَانُوْا يَعْرِشُوْنَ‏(137)\nWAAWRASNAA QAWMAZ LAZEENA KAANOO YUSTAZA’AFOONA MASHAAREQA ARZE WAMAGHAAREBAHAA LATEE BAARAKNAA FEEHAA WATAMMAT KALEMATU RABBEKA AL-HUSNAA A’LAA BANEE AESRAAEELA BEMAA SABAROO WADAMMARNAA MAA KAANA YASNAU’U FIRA’WNO WA QAWMOHU WA MAA KAANOO YAA’RESHOONA.\nAnd We made a people, considered weak (and of no account), inheritors of lands in both east and west, - lands whereon We sent down Our blessings. The fair promise of thy Lord was fulfilled for the Children of Israel, because they had patience and constancy, and We levelled to the ground the great works and fine buildings which Pharaoh and his people erected (with such pride). \nوَجَاوَزْنَا بِبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَاۤءِيْلَ الْبَحْرَ فَاَ تَوْا عَلٰى قَوْمٍ يَّعْكُفُوْنَ عَلٰٓى اَصْنَامٍ لَّهُمْ ۚ قَالُوْا يٰمُوْسَى اجْعَلْ لَّنَاۤ اِلٰهًا كَمَا لَهُمْ اٰلِهَةٌ  ؕ قَالَ اِنَّكُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(138)\nWAJAAWAZNAA BE-BANEE AESRAAEELA BAHRA FA ATAW A’LAA QAWMIN YYAA’KUFOONA A’LAA AASNAAMIN LAHUM QAALOO YAA MOOSAL A’L LANAA ELAAHANW KAMAA LAHUM AAALEHATUN QAALA INNAKUM QAWMUN TAJHALOON.\nWe took the Children of Israel (with safety) across the sea. They came upon a people devoted entirely to some idols they had. They said: “O Moses! fashion for us a god like unto the gods they have.” He said: “Surely ye are a people without knowledge. \nاِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَۤاءِ مُتَبَّرٌ مَّا هُمْ فِيْهِ وَبٰطِلٌ مَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(139)\nINNAL HAAOOLAAA-E MUTABBARUN MAA HUM FEEHE WABAATELUN MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\n“As to these folk, the cult they are in is (but) a fragment of a ruin, and vain is the (worship) which they practise.” \nقَالَ اَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ اَبْغِيْكُمْ اِلٰهًا وَّهُوَ فَضَّلَكُمْ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(140)\nQAALA AAGHAYRA LAAHE AABGHEEKUM ELAAHANW WA FAZZALAKUM A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nHe said: “Shall I seek for you a god other than the (true) Allah, when it is Allah Who hath endowed you with gifts above the nations?” \nوَاِذْ اَنْجَيْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ اٰلِ فِرْعَوْنَ يَسُوْمُوْنَكُمْ سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ ۚ يُقَتِّلُوْنَ اَبْنَآءَكُمْ وَ يَسْتَحْيُوْنَ نِسَآءَكُمْ ؕ وَفِىْ ذٰ لِكُمْ بَلَاۤ ءٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ عَظِيْمٌ‏(141)\nWA IZ AANJAYNAAKUM MIN AALE FIR-A’WNA YASOOMOONAKUM SOOO-AL A’ZAABE YUQATTELOONA ABNAAA-AKUM WA YASTAHYOONA NESAAAKUM WA FEE ZAA ZAALEKUM BALAA UN MIN RABBEKUM A’ZEEM.\nAnd remember We rescued you from Pharaoh's people, who afflicted you with the worst of penalties, who slew your male children and saved alive your females: in that was a momentous trial from your Lord. \nوَوٰعَدْنَا مُوْسٰى ثَلٰثِيْنَ لَيْلَةً وَّاَتْمَمْنٰهَا بِعَشْرٍ فَتَمَّ مِيْقَاتُ رَبِّهٖۤ اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً  ۚ وَقَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَخِيْهِ هٰرُوْنَ اخْلُفْنِىْ فِىْ قَوْمِىْ وَاَصْلِحْ وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(142)\nWA WAA-A’DNAA MOOSAA SALAASEENA LAYLATAN WWAATMAMNAAHAA BE-A’SRINW FATAMMA MEEQAATU RABBEHI ARBA-E’ENA LAYLATAN WA QAALA MOOSAA LE-AKHEEHE AALO AKHLUFNEAA FEE QAWMEE WAASLEH WA LAA TATTABEA’ SABEELA MUFSEDEEN.\n We appointed for Moses thirty nights, and completed (the period) with ten (more): thus was completed the term (of communion) with his Lord, forty nights. And Moses had charged his brother Aaron (before he went up): “Act for me amongst my people: Do right, and follow not the way of those who do mischief.” \nوَلَمَّا جَآءَ مُوْسٰى لِمِيْقَاتِنَا وَكَلَّمَهٗ رَبُّهٗ ۙ قَالَ رَبِّ اَرِنِىْۤ اَنْظُرْ اِلَيْكَ ؕ قَالَ لَنْ تَرٰٮنِىْ وَلٰكِنِ انْظُرْ اِلَى الْجَبَلِ فَاِنِ اسْتَقَرَّ مَكَانَهٗ فَسَوْفَ تَرٰٮنِىْ ۚ فَلَمَّا تَجَلّٰى رَبُّهٗ لِلْجَبَلِ جَعَلَهٗ دَكًّا وَّخَرَّ مُوْسٰى صَعِقًا ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبْحٰنَكَ تُبْتُ اِلَيْكَ وَاَنَا اَوَّلُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(143)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A MOOSAA LEMEEQAATENAA WAKALLAMAH RABBOHU QAALA RABBE ARENEE AANZUR ELAYKA QAALA LAN TARAANEAA LAAKENIKH ANZUR ELAL AL-JABALE FA-ENIN ASTAQARRA MAKAANAHU FA-SAWFA TARAANEAA FALAMMAA TAJALLAA RABBOHU LIL-JABALE JAA’ALAH DAKKANW WWAKHARRA MOOSAA SAE’EQAN FALAMMAA AAFAAQA QAALA SUBHAANAKA TUBTU ELAYKA ANAT AAWLU MOAMENEEN.\nWhen Moses came to the place appointed by Us, and his Lord addressed him, He said: “O my Lord! show (Thyself) to me, that I may look upon thee.” Allah said: “By no means canst thou see Me (direct); But look upon the mount; if it abide in its place, then shalt thou see Me.” When his Lord manifested His glory on the Mount, He made it as dust. And Moses fell down in a swoon. When he recovered his senses he said: “Glory be to Thee! to Thee I turn in repentance, and I am the first to believe.” \nقَالَ يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِنِّى اصْطَفَيْتُكَ عَلَى النَّاسِ بِرِسٰلٰتِىْ وَ بِكَلَامِىْ ۖ  فَخُذْ مَاۤ اٰتَيْتُكَ وَكُنْ مِّنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(144)\nQAALA MOOSAA AENNEAA ASTAFAYTUKA A’LAL NAASE BERESAALAATEAA WA BEKALAAMEAA FA-KHUZ MAA AAATAYTUKA WA KUN MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\n(Allah) said: “O Moses! I have chosen thee above (other) men, by the mission I (have given thee) and the words I (have spoken to thee): take then the (revelation) which I give thee, and be of those who give thanks.” \nوَكَتَبْنَا لَهٗ فِى الْاَلْوَاحِ مِنْ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ مَّوْعِظَةً وَّتَفْصِيْلًا لِّكُلِّ شَىْءٍ ۚ فَخُذْهَا بِقُوَّةٍ وَّاْمُرْ قَوْمَكَ يَاْخُذُوْا بِاَحْسَنِهَا ؕ سَاُورِيْكُمْ دَارَ الْفٰسِقِيْنَ‏(145)\nWAKATABNAA LAHU FIL AL-AALWAAHE MIN KULLE SHAY-IN MMAWE’EZATAN WWATAFSEELAN LEKULLE SHAY-IN FAKHUZHAA BE-QUWWATINW WWAAMUR QAWMAKA YAAKHUZOOA BEAAHSANEHAA SAAWREEKUM DAARA FAASEQEEN.\nAnd We ordained laws for him in the tablets in all matters, both commanding and explaining all things, (and said): “Take and hold these with firmness, and enjoin thy people to hold fast by the best in the precepts: soon shall I show you the homes of the wicked, (How they lie desolate).” \nسَاَصْرِفُ عَنْ اٰيٰتِىَ الَّذِيْنَ يَتَكَبَّرُوْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ ؕ وَاِنْ يَّرَوْا كُلَّ اٰيَةٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْا بِهَا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّرَوْا سَبِيْلَ الرُّشْدِ لَا يَتَّخِذُوْهُ سَبِيْلًا ۚ وَّاِنْ يَّرَوْا سَبِيْلَ الْغَىِّ يَتَّخِذُوْهُ سَبِيْلًا ؕ ذٰ لِكَ بِاَنَّهُمْ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَكَانُوْا عَنْهَا غٰفِلِيْنَ‏(146)\nSAASREFU A’N AAAYAATEAAA LAZEENA YATAKABBAROONA FIL ARZE BEGHAYRIL HAQQE WA YYARAWA KULLA AAYATIM LAA YOAMENOO BEHAA WA YYARAWA SABEELA AR-RUSHDE LAA YATTAKHEZOOHU SABEELAA WA YYARAWA SABEELA GHAYY YATTAKHEZOOHU SABEELAA ZAA LEKA BE-ANNAHUM KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WA KAANOO A’NHAA GHAAFELEENA.\nThose who behave arrogantly on the earth in defiance of right - them will I turn away from My signs: Even if they see all the signs, they will not believe in them; and if they see the way of right conduct, they will not adopt it as the way; but if they see the way of error, that is the way they will adopt. For they have rejected our signs, and failed to take warning from them. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَلِقَآءِ الْاٰخِرَةِ حَبِطَتْ اَعْمَالُهُمْؕ هَلْ يُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(147)\nWAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WALEQAAE AAKHERATE HABETAT AAA’MAALUHUM HAL YUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThose who reject Our signs and the meeting in the Hereafter, vain are their deeds: Can they expect to be rewarded except as they have wrought? \nوَاتَّخَذَ قَوْمُ مُوْسٰى مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ مِنْ حُلِيِّهِمْ عِجْلًا جَسَدًا لَّهٗ خُوَارٌ ؕ اَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّهٗ لَا يُكَلِّمُهُمْ وَلَا يَهْدِيْهِمْ سَبِيْلًا ۘ اِتَّخَذُوْهُ وَكَانُوْا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‏(148)\nWA TAKHAZA QAWMO MOOSAA MIN BA’DEHI MIN HULEEHEM E’EJLAN JASADAN LAHU KHOOARUN ALAM YARAW ANNAHU LAA YUKALLEMUHUM WA LAA YAHDEEHEM SABEELAA AETTAKHAZOOHU WA KAANOO ZAALEMEEN.\nThe people of Moses made, in his absence, out of their ornaments, the image of calf, (for worship): it seemed to low: did they not see that it could neither speak to them, nor show them the way? They took it for worship and they did wrong. \nوَلَمَّا سُقِطَ فِىْۤ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَرَاَوْا اَنَّهُمْ قَدْ ضَلُّوْا ۙ قَالُوْا لَئِنْ لَّمْ يَرْحَمْنَا رَبُّنَا وَيَغْفِرْ لَنَا لَنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(149)\nWA LAMMAA SUQETA FEE AYDEEHIM WA RA-AW ANNAHUM QAD ZALLOOA QAALOO LAIL LAM YARHAMNAA RABBONAA WA YAGHFIR LANAA LANAKOONANNA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nWhen they repented, and saw that they had erred, they said: “If our Lord have not mercy upon us and forgive us, we shall indeed be of those who perish.” \nوَلَمَّا رَجَعَ مُوْسٰٓى اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ غَضْبَانَ اَسِفًا ۙ قَالَ بِئْسَمَا خَلَفْتُمُوْنِىْ مِنْۢ بَعْدِىْ ۚ اَعَجِلْتُمْ اَمْرَ رَبِّكُمْ ۚ وَاَلْقَى الْاَلْوَاحَ وَاَخَذَ بِرَاْسِ اَخِيْهِ يَجُرُّهٗۤ اِلَيْهِؕ قَالَ ابْنَ اُمَّ اِنَّ الْقَوْمَ اسْتَضْعَفُوْنِىْ وَكَادُوْا يَقْتُلُوْنَنِىْ ۖ  فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِىَ الْاَعْدَآءَ وَ لَا تَجْعَلْنِىْ مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(150)\nWA LAMMAA RAJAA’A MOOSAA ELAA QAWMEHI GHAZBAANA AASEFAN QAALA BEASAMASH KHALAFTUMOONEAA MIN BAA’DEAA AAA’AJELTUM AAMRA RABBEKUM WAALQAA AL-AALWAAHA WAAKHAZA BERAASE AKHEEHE YAJURRUH AELAYHE QAALA NA AUMMA INNAL QAWMAZ ASTAZA’AFOONEAA WA KAADOO YAQTULOONANEAA FALAA TUSHMET BEAAA AL-AAA’DAAA WA LAA TAJA’ALNEAA LAAHA QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nWhen Moses came back to his people, angry and grieved, he said: “Evil it is that ye have done in my place in my absence: did ye make haste to bring on the judgment of your Lord?” He put down the tablets, seized his brother by (the hair of) his head, and dragged him to him. Aaron said: “Son of my mother! the people did indeed reckon me as naught, and went near to slaying me! Make not the enemies rejoice over my misfortune, nor count thou me amongst the people of sin.” \nقَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِىْ وَلِاَخِىْ وَ اَدْخِلْنَا فِىْ رَحْمَتِكَ ۖ  وَاَنْتَ اَرْحَمُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(151)\nQAALA RABBE FIR LEE WALEAAKHEAA WA AADKHELNAA FEE RAHMATEKA WA ANTA AARHAMU AR-RAAHEMEENA.\nMoses prayed: “O my Lord! forgive me and my brother! admit us to Thy mercy! for Thou art the Most Merciful of those who show mercy!” \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوا الْعِجْلَ سَيَنَالُهُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمْ وَذِلَّةٌ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ؕ وَكَذٰلِكَ نَجْزِىْ الْمُفْتَرِيْنَ‏(152)\nINNAL LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA I’JLA SAYANAALUHUM GHAZABUN MIN RABBEHIM WAZELLATUN FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA KAZAALEKA NAJZEAA AL-MUFTAREENA.\nThose who took the calf (for worship) will indeed be overwhelmed with wrath from their Lord, and with shame in this life: thus do We recompense those who invent (falsehoods). \nوَالَّذِيْنَ عَمِلُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ ثُمَّ تَابُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا وَاٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ رَبَّكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهَا لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(153)\nWAL LAZEENA A’MELUS SAYYE-AATE SUMMA TAABOO MIN BAA’DEHAA WA AAMANOO INNAL RABBAKA MIN BAA’DEHAA LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nBut those who do wrong but repent thereafter and (truly) believe, verily thy Lord is thereafter Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَلَمَّا سَكَتَ عَنْ مُّوْسَى الْغَضَبُ اَخَذَ الْاَلْوَاحَ ۖ  وَفِىْ نُسْخَتِهَا هُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِرَبِّهِمْ يَرْهَبُوْنَ‏(154)\nWA LAMMAA SAKATA A’N MMOOSAA AL-GHAZABU AAKHAZA AL-AALWAAHA WA FEE NUSKHATEHAA HODAM WA RAHMATUL LIL-LAZEENA HUM LE-RABBEHIM YARHABOONA.\nWhen the anger of Moses was appeased, he took up the tablets: in the writing thereon was guidance and Mercy for such as fear their Lord. \nوَاخْتَارَ مُوْسٰى قَوْمَهٗ سَبْعِيْنَ رَجُلًا لِّمِيْقَاتِنَا ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ قَالَ رَبِّ لَوْ شِئْتَ اَهْلَكْتَهُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُ وَاِيَّاىَ ؕ اَ تُهْلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ السُّفَهَآءُ مِنَّا ۚ اِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا فِتْنَتُكَ ؕ تُضِلُّ بِهَا مَنْ تَشَآءُ وَتَهْدِىْ مَنْ تَشَآءُ ؕ اَنْتَ وَلِيُّنَا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْغَافِرِيْنَ‏(155)\nWAAKHTAARA MOOSAA QAWMAH SABE’EENA RAJULAN LLEMEEQAATENAA FALAMMAA AAKHAZATHUMU RAJFATO QAALA RABBE LAW SHETA AAHLAKTAHUM MIN QABLO WA IYYAAYA AATUHLEKUNAA BEMAA FA-A’LA WA MINNAA IN HEYA ILLAA FETNATUKA TUZELLU BEHAA MAN TASHAAA WA TAHDEE MAN TASHAAA ANTA WALEENAA FAGH-FIR LANAA HAMNAA WA ANTA KHAYRUR AL-GHAAFEREENA.\nAnd Moses chose seventy of his people for Our place of meeting: when they were seized with violent quaking, he prayed: “O my Lord! if it had been Thy will Thou couldst have destroyed, long before, both them and me: wouldst Thou destroy us for the deeds of the foolish ones among us? this is no more than Thy trial: by it Thou causest whom Thou wilt to stray, and Thou leadest whom Thou wilt into the right path. Thou art our Protector: so forgive us and give us Thy mercy; for Thou art the best of those who forgive. \nوَاكْتُبْ لَنَا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَّفِى الْاٰخِرَةِ اِنَّا هُدْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ ؕ قَالَ عَذَابِىْۤ اُصِيْبُ بِهٖ مَنْ اَشَآءُ ۚ وَرَحْمَتِىْ وَسِعَتْ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ ؕ فَسَاَكْتُبُهَا لِلَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَ وَيُؤْتُوْنَ الزَّكٰوةَ وَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِاٰيٰتِنَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ ۚ‏(156)\nWAAKTUB LANAA FEE HAAZEHE DUNYAA HASANATANW WA FIL AAKHERATE INNAA HUDNAA ELAYKA QAALA A’AZAABEAA AUSEEBU BEHI MAN AASHAAU WARAHMATEAA WASEA’AT KULLA SHAY-IN FASAAKTUBUHAA LILLAZEENA YATTAQOON WA YOATOONAZ ZAKAATA WAL LAZEENA HUM BE-AAYAATENAA YOAMENOONA.\n “And ordain for us that which is good, in this life and in the Hereafter: for we have turned unto Thee.” He said: “With My punishment I visit whom I will; but My mercy extendeth to all things. That (mercy) I shall ordain for those who do right, and practise regular charity, and those who believe in Our signs;- \nاَ لَّذِيْنَ يَتَّبِعُوْنَ الرَّسُوْلَ النَّبِىَّ الْاُمِّىَّ الَّذِىْ يَجِدُوْنَهٗ مَكْتُوْبًا عِنْدَهُمْ فِى التَّوْرٰٮةِ وَالْاِنْجِيْلِ يَاْمُرُهُمْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَيَنْهٰٮهُمْ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ وَيُحِلُّ لَهُمُ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَيُحَرِّمُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْخَبٰۤئِثَ وَيَضَعُ عَنْهُمْ اِصْرَهُمْ وَالْاَغْلٰلَ الَّتِىْ كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ ؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِهٖ وَعَزَّرُوْهُ وَنَصَرُوْهُ وَ اتَّبَعُوا النُّوْرَ الَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ مَعَهٗ ۤ ۙ اُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(157)\nLAZEENA YATTABEU’OONA YATTABE-U’R NABIYYA AL-AUMMEAAAA LAZEE YAJEDOONAH MAKTOOBAN E’ENDAHUM FIL WA WA INJEELE YAAMURUHUM BIL-MA’ROOF WAYANHAAHUM A’NIL AL-MUNKARE WAYUHELLU LAHOMUL AT-TAYBAATE WAYUHARREMU A’LAYHEMUL AL-KHABAAESA WAYAZAU’U A’NHUM AESRAHUM WAL AAGHLAALA LATEE KAANAT A’LAYHIM FAL LAZEENA AAMANOO BEHI WAA’AZZAROOHU WANASAROOHU WA ATTABAU’OOA AN-NOORA LAZEE UNZELA MA-A’HU AOOLAAEKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\n“Those who follow the messenger, the unlettered Prophet, whom they find mentioned in their own (scriptures), in the law and the Gospel;- for he commands them what is just and forbids them what is evil; he allows them as lawful what is good (and pure) and prohibits them from what is bad (and impure); He releases them from their heavy burdens and from the yokes that are upon them. So it is those who believe in him, honour him, help him, and follow the light which is sent down with him, it is they who will prosper.” \nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اِنِّىْ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ اِلَيْكُمْ جَمِيْعَاْ ۨالَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ فَاٰمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهِ النَّبِىِّ الْاُمِّىِّ الَّذِىْ يُؤْمِنُ بِاللّٰهِ وَكَلِمٰتِهٖ وَاتَّبِعُوْهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(158)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL NAASO INNEE RASOOLAL LAAHE ELAYKUM JAMEEA’AA LAZEE LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA YOHYEE WA YOMEETO FA AAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WARASOOLEHE NESAAA-AN AL-AUMMEAAAE LAZEE BIL LAAHE BIL-LAAHE WAKALEMAATEH WAATTABEU’OOHU LA-A’LLAKUM TAHTADOON.\nSay: “O men! I am sent unto you all, as the Messenger of Allah, to Whom belongeth the dominion of the heavens and the earth: there is no god but He: it is He That giveth both life and death. So believe in Allah and His Messenger, the Unlettered Prophet, who believeth in Allah and His words: follow him that (so) ye may be guided.” \nوَ مِنْ قَوْمِ مُوْسٰٓى اُمَّةٌ يَّهْدُوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ وَبِهٖ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(159)\nWA MIN QAWME MOOSAA UMMATUN YYAHDOONA BIL-HAQQE WA BEHI YAA’DELOONA.\nOf the people of Moses there is a section who guide and do justice in the light of truth. \nوَقَطَّعْنٰهُمُ اثْنَتَىْ عَشْرَةَ اَسْبَاطًا اُمَمًا ؕ وَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى اِذِ اسْتَسْقٰٮهُ قَوْمُهٗۤ اَنِ اضْرِبْ بِّعَصَاكَ الْحَجَرَ ۚ فَاْنۢبَجَسَتْ مِنْهُ اثْنَتَا عَشْرَةَ عَيْنًا ؕ قَدْ عَلِمَ كُلُّ اُنَاسٍ مَّشْرَبَهُمْؕ وَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الْغَمَامَ وَاَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوٰىؕ كُلُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا رَزَقْنٰكُمْؕ وَ مَا ظَلَمُوْنَا وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(160)\nWAQATTAA’NAAHUMU ASNATAA A’SHRATA AASBAATAN AUMAMAN WA AWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA EZIM ASTASQAAHU QAWMOHU SAALEHAN AZREB BE-A’SAAKAL AL-HAJARA FAANBAJASAT MINHO NATAA A’SHRATA A’YNAN QAD A’LEMA KULLO ONAASIM MASHRABAHUM WA ZALLALNAA A’LAYHEMUL GHAMAAMA WA ANZALNAA A’LAYHEMUL MANNA WAS SALWAA KOLOO MIN TAYYEBAATE MAA RAZAQNAAKUM WA MAA ZALAMOONAA WA LAAKIL KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nWe divided them into twelve tribes or nations. We directed Moses by inspiration, when his (thirsty) people asked him for water: “Strike the rock with thy staff”: out of it there gushed forth twelve springs: Each group knew its own place for water. We gave them the shade of clouds, and sent down to them manna and quails, (saying): “Eat of the good things We have provided for you”: (but they rebelled); to Us they did no harm, but they harmed their own souls. \nوَاِذْ قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اسْكُنُوْا هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةَ وَكُلُوْا مِنْهَا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمْ وَقُوْلُوْا حِطَّةٌ وَّادْخُلُوا الْبَابَ سُجَّدًا نَّغْفِرْ لَكُمْ خَطِيْٓئٰتِكُمْ ؕ سَنَزِيْدُ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(161)\nWA IZ QEELA LAHOMUL ASKUNOOA HAAZEHE QARYATA WA KOLOO MINHAA HAYSO SHEATUM WA QOOLOO HITTATUN WAD-KHOLUL BAABA SUJJADANW NAGHFIR LAKUM KHATEEAATEKUM SANAZEEDU MOHSENEEN.\nAnd remember it was said to them: “Dwell in this town and eat therein as ye wish, but say the word of humility and enter the gate in a posture of humility: We shall forgive you your faults; We shall increase (the portion of) those who do good.” \nفَبَدَّلَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ قَوْلًا غَيْرَ الَّذِىْ قِيْلَ لَهُمْ فَاَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِجْزًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(162)\nFA-BADDALAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO MINHUM QAWLAM GHAYRA LAZEE QEELA LAHUM FA-ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM RIJZAM MENAL SAMAAA-E BEMAA KAANOO YAZLEMOON.\nBut the transgressors among them changed the word from that which had been given them so we sent on them a plague from heaven. For that they repeatedly transgressed. \nوَسْئَلْهُمْ عَنِ الْقَرْيَةِ الَّتِىْ كَانَتْ حَاضِرَةَ الْبَحْرِۘ اِذْ يَعْدُوْنَ فِى السَّبْتِ اِذْ تَاْتِيْهِمْ حِيْتَانُهُمْ يَوْمَ سَبْتِهِمْ شُرَّعًا وَّيَوْمَ لَا يَسْبِتُوْنَ ۙ لَا تَاْتِيْهِمْ ۛۚ كَذٰلِكَ ۛۚ نَبْلُوْهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(163)\nWASALHUM A’NIL QARYAH LATEE KAANAT HAAZERATA BAHRE IZ YAA’DOONA FIL SABTE IZ TAA-TEEHIM HEETAANUHUM YAWMA SABTEHEM SHURRAA’AN WWAYAWMA LAA YASBETOONA LAA TAA-TEEHIM KAZAALEKA NABLOOHUM BEMAA KAANOO YAFSOQOON.\nAsk them concerning the town standing close by the sea. Behold! they transgressed in the matter of the Sabbath. For on the day of their Sabbath their fish did come to them, openly holding up their heads, but on the day they had no Sabbath, they came not: thus did We make a trial of them, for they were given to transgression. \nوَاِذْ قَالَتْ اُمَّةٌ مِّنْهُمْ لِمَ تَعِظُوْنَ قَوْمَاْ  ۙ اۨللّٰهُ مُهْلِكُهُمْ اَوْ مُعَذِّبُهُمْ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ قَالُوْا مَعْذِرَةً اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ وَلَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(164)\nWA IZ QAALAT UMMATUN MINHUM LEMA TAE’EZOONA QAWMAA LAAHO MUHLEKUHUM AW MUA’AZZEBUHUM A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA QAALOO MAA’ZERATAN ELAA RABBEKUM WA LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\nWhen some of them said: “Why do ye preach to a people whom Allah will destroy or visit with a terrible punishment?”- said the preachers:” To discharge our duty to your Lord, and perchance they may fear Him.” \nفَلَمَّا نَسُوْا مَا ذُكِّرُوْا بِهٖۤ اَنْجَيْنَا الَّذِيْنَ يَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ السُّوْۤءِ وَاَخَذْنَا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا بِعَذَابٍۭ بَئِيْسٍۭ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(165)\nFALAMMAA NASOOA MAA ZUKKEROOA BEHI AANJAYNAA LAZEENA YANHAWNA A’NIL AS-SOOE AKHAZNAA LAZEENA ZALAMOO BE-A’ZAABIN BAEESIN BEMAA KAANOO YAFSOQOON.\nWhen they disregarded the warnings that had been given them, We rescued those who forbade Evil; but We visited the wrong-doers with a grievous punishment because they were given to transgression. \nفَلَمَّا عَتَوْا عَنْ مَّا نُهُوْا عَنْهُ قُلْنَا لَهُمْ كُوْنُوْا قِرَدَةً خٰسِئِیْنَ‏(166)\nFALAMMAA A’ATAWA A’N MAA NUHOOA A’NHO QULNAL LAHUM KOONOO QERADATAN KHAASEEENA.\nWhen in their insolence they transgressed (all) prohibitions, We said to them: “Be ye apes, despised and rejected.” \nوَاِذْ تَاَذَّنَ رَبُّكَ لَيَبْعَثَنَّ عَلَيْهِمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ مَنْ يَّسُوْمُهُمْ سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَسَرِيْعُ الْعِقَابِ  ۖۚ وَاِنَّهٗ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(167)\nWA IZ TAAZZANA RABBOKA LAYABA’ASANNA A’LAYHIM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE MAN YYASOOMUHUM SOOO-AL A’ZAABE INNAL RABBAKA LASAREEU’U E’QAAB WA INNAHU LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nBehold! thy Lord did declare that He would send against them, to the Day of Judgment, those who would afflict them with grievous penalty. Thy Lord is quick in retribution, but He is also Oft-forgiving, Most Merciful. \nوَقَطَّعْنٰهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اُمَمًا ۚ مِنْهُمُ الصّٰلِحُوْنَ وَمِنْهُمْ دُوْنَ ذٰ لِكَ وَبَلَوْنٰهُمْ بِالْحَسَنٰتِ وَالسَّيِّاٰتِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(168)\nWAQATTAA’NAAHUM FIL ARZE AUMAMAN MENHUMU AS-SAALEHOONA WA MINHUM DOONA ZAA LEKA WABALAWNAAHUM BIL-HASANAATE WA SAYYE-AATE LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nWe broke them up into sections on this earth. There are among them some that are the righteous, and some that are the opposite. We have tried them with both prosperity and adversity: In order that they might turn (to us). \nفَخَلَفَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ خَلْفٌ وَّرِثُوا الْكِتٰبَ يَاْخُذُوْنَ عَرَضَ هٰذَا الْاَدْنٰى وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ سَيُغْفَرُ لَنَا ۚ وَاِنْ يَّاْتِهِمْ عَرَضٌ مِّثْلُهٗ يَاْخُذُوْهُ ؕ اَلَمْ يُؤْخَذْ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّيْثَاقُ الْكِتٰبِ اَنْ لَّا يَقُوْلُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ اِلَّا الْحَقَّ وَدَرَسُوْا مَا فِيْهِ ؕ وَالدَّارُ الْاٰخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ يَتَّقُوْنَ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(169)\nFAKHALAFA MIN BA’DEHIM KHALFUN WWARESOOA KETAABA YAAKHUZOONA A’ARAZA HAAZAA AL-AADNAA WA YAQOOLOONA SAYUGHFARU LANAA WA YYAATEHEM A’ARAZUN MMESLUH YAAKHUZOOHU ALAM YUKHAZ A’LAYHIM MMEESAAQU KETAABE AN LAA YAQOOLOOA A’LAL LAAHE ILLAA HAQQA WADARASOOA MAA FEEHE WA DAARUL AAKHERATO KHAYRUL LIL-LAZEENA YATTAQOON AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAfter them succeeded an (evil) generation: They inherited the Book, but they chose (for themselves) the vanities of this world, saying (for excuse): “(Everything) will be forgiven us.” (Even so), if similar vanities came their way, they would (again) seize them. Was not the covenant of the Book taken from them, that they would not ascribe to Allah anything but the truth? and they study what is in the Book. But best for the righteous is the home in the Hereafter. Will ye not understand? \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُمَسِّكُوْنَ بِالْكِتٰبِ وَاَقَامُوا الصَّلٰوةَ ؕ اِنَّا لَا نُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُصْلِحِيْنَ‏(170)\nWAL LAZEENA YUMASSEKOONA BE-KETAABE WA AQAAMUS SALAATA INNAA LAA NUZEEU’U AJRA MUSLEHEEN.\nAs to those who hold fast by the Book and establish regular prayer, never shall We suffer the reward of the righteous to perish. \nوَاِذْ نَتَقْنَا الْجَبَلَ فَوْقَهُمْ كَاَنَّهٗ ظُلَّةٌ وَّظَنُّوْۤا اَنَّهٗ وَاقِعٌ ۢ بِهِمْ ۚ خُذُوْا مَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰكُمْ بِقُوَّةٍ وَّاذْكُرُوْا مَا فِيْهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(171)\nWA IZ NATAQNAA AL-JABALA FAWQAHUM KA-ANNAHU ZULLATUN WWAZANNOOA ANNAHU WAAQEA’UN BEHIM KHOZOO MAA AATAYNAAKUM BE-QUWWATINW WAZ KOROO MAA FEEHE LA-A’LLAKUM TATTAQOON.\n When We shook the Mount over them, as if it had been a canopy, and they thought it was going to fall on them (We said): “Hold firmly to what We have given you, and bring (ever) to remembrance what is therein; perchance ye may fear Allah.” \nوَ اِذْ اَخَذَ رَبُّكَ مِنْۢ بَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ مِنْ ظُهُوْرِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ وَ اَشْهَدَهُمْ عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ ۚ اَلَسْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى ۛۚ شَهِدْنَا ۛۚ اَنْ تَقُوْلُوْا يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ اِنَّا كُنَّا عَنْ هٰذَا غٰفِلِيْنَ ۙ‏(172)\nWA IZ AAKHAZA RABBOKA MIN BANEE AADAMAL MIN ZOHOOREHIM ZURRIYYATAHUM WA AASHHADAHUM A’LAA ANFOSEHIM AALASTU BE-RABBEKUM QAALOO BALAA SHAHIDNAA AN TAQOOLOO YAWMA QEYAAMATE INNAA KUNNAA A’N HAAZAA GHAAFELEENA.\nWhen thy Lord drew forth from the Children of Adam - from their loins - their descendants, and made them testify concerning themselves, (saying): “Am I not your Lord (who cherishes and sustains you)?”- They said: “Yea! We do testify!” (This), lest ye should say on the Day of Judgment: “Of this we were never mindful”: \nاَوْ تَقُوْلُوْۤا اِنَّمَاۤ اَشْرَكَ اٰبَآؤُنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ وَكُنَّا ذُرِّيَّةً مِّنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْۚ اَفَتُهْلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(173)\nAW TAQOOLOO INNAMAA AASHRAKA AAABAAUNAA MIN QABLO KUNNAA ZURREETAN MIN BA’DEHIM AAFATUHLEKUNAA BEMAA FA-A’LA MUBTELOON.\nOr lest ye should say: “Our fathers before us may have taken false gods, but we are (their) descendants after them: wilt Thou then destroy us because of the deeds of men who were futile?” \nوَكَذٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ الْاٰيٰتِ وَلَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(174)\nWA KAZAALEKA NOFASSELUL AAYAATE WA LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nThus do We explain the signs in detail; and perchance they may turn (unto Us). \nوَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَاَ الَّذِىْۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُ اٰيٰتِنَا فَانْسَلَخَ مِنْهَا فَاَتْبَعَهُ الشَّيْطٰنُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْغٰوِيْنَ‏(175)\nWAATLU A’LAYHIM NABAAALLAZEAA AATAYNAAHO AAYAATENAA FAANSALAKHA MINHAA FAATBAA’AHU SHAYTAANO FA KAANA MENAL AL-GHAAWEENA.\nRelate to them the story of the man to whom We sent Our signs, but he passed them by: so Satan followed him up, and he went astray. \nوَلَوْ شِئْنَا لَرَفَعْنٰهُ بِهَا وَلٰكِنَّهٗۤ اَخْلَدَ اِلَى الْاَرْضِ وَاتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ ۚ فَمَثَلُهٗ كَمَثَلِ الْكَلْبِ ۚ اِنْ تَحْمِلْ عَلَيْهِ يَلْهَثْ اَوْ تَتْرُكْهُ يَلْهَث ؕ ذٰ لِكَ مَثَلُ الْقَوْمِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا ۚ فَاقْصُصِ الْقَصَصَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(176)\nWA LAW SHE’NAA LARAFAA’NAAHU BEHAA WALAAKENNAH AAKHLADA ELAL ARZE WA TABA-A’L HAWHU AAKHER KAMASALIL AL-KALBE IN KAMAA A’LAYHE YALHAS AW TATRUKHU YALHAS ZAA LEKA MASALUL QAWMIL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA FAAQSUSE QASASA LA-A’LLAHUM YATAFAKKAROON.\nIf it had been Our will, We should have elevated him with Our signs; but he inclined to the earth, and followed his own vain desires. His similitude is that of a dog: if you attack him, he lolls out his tongue, or if you leave him alone, he (still) lolls out his tongue. That is the similitude of those who reject Our signs; So relate the story; perchance they may reflect. \nسَآءَ مَثَلَاْ ۨالْقَوْمُ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَاَنْفُسَهُمْ كَانُوْا يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(177)\nSAAA-A MASALAA AL-QAWMU LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA WA ANFOSAHUM KAANOO YAZLEMOON.\nEvil as an example are people who reject Our signs and wrong their own souls. \nمَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَهُوَ الْمُهْتَدِىْۚ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلْ فَاُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(178)\nMAN YYAHDE LAAHO FAHOWA AL-MUHTADEAA WA MAN YYUZLEL FAAWLAAEKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nWhom Allah doth guide, he is on the right path: whom He rejects from His guidance, such are the persons who perish. \nوَلَقَدْ ذَرَاْنَا لِجَهَنَّمَ كَثِيْرًا مِّنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْاِنْسِ ۖ  لَهُمْ قُلُوْبٌ لَّا يَفْقَهُوْنَ بِهَا  وَلَهُمْ اَعْيُنٌ لَّا يُبْصِرُوْنَ بِهَا  وَلَهُمْ اٰذَانٌ لَّا يَسْمَعُوْنَ بِهَا ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ كَالْاَنْعَامِ بَلْ هُمْ اَضَلُّ ؕ اُولٰۤئِكَ هُمُ الْغٰفِلُوْنَ‏(179)\nWA LAQAD ZARAANAA LE-JAHANNAMA KASEERAA MENAL JINNE WAL INSE LAHUM QULOOBUN LAA YAFQAHOON BEHAA WA LAHUM AAA’YUNUN LAA YUBSEROON BEHAA WA LAHUM AAAZAANUN LAA YAS-MA-O’ONA BEHAA AOOLAAEKA KAALAANA’AAME BAL HUM AZALLO AOOLAAEKA HOMUL AL-GHAAFELOONA.\nMany are the Jinns and men we have made for Hell: They have hearts wherewith they understand not, eyes wherewith they see not, and ears wherewith they hear not. They are like cattle, nay more misguided: for they are heedless (of warning). \nوَلِلّٰهِ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى فَادْعُوْهُ بِهَا وَذَرُوا الَّذِيْنَ يُلْحِدُوْنَ فِىْۤ اَسْمَآئِهٖ ؕ سَيُجْزَوْنَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(180)\nLILLAAHE ASMAA-UL AL-HUSNAA FAADU’OOHU BEHAA LAAHE LAZEENA YULHEDOONA FEE AASMAAEH SAYUJZAWNA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThe most beautiful names belong to Allah: so call on him by them; but shun such men as use profanity in his names: for what they do, they will soon be requited. \nوَمِمَّنْ خَلَقْنَاۤ اُمَّةٌ يَّهْدُوْنَ بِالْحَقِّ وَبِهٖ يَعْدِلُوْنَ‏(181)\nWA MIMMAN KHALAQNAL UMMATUN YYAHDOONA BIL-HAQQE WA BEHI YAA’DELOONA.\nOf those We have created are people who direct (others) with truth. And dispense justice therewith. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَذَّبُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُمْ مِّنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ ۖ  ۚ‏(182)\nWAL LAZEENA KAZZABOO BE-AAYAATENAA SANASTADREJUHUM MIN HAYSO LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThose who reject Our signs, We shall gradually visit with punishment, in ways they perceive not; \nوَاُمْلِىْ لَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّ كَيْدِىْ مَتِيْنٌ‏(183)\nWAAMLEAA LAHUM INNAL KAYDEAA MATEENUN.\nRespite will I grant unto them: for My scheme is strong (and unfailing). \nاَوَلَمْ يَتَفَكَّرُوْا مَا بِصَاحِبِهِمْ مِّنْ جِنَّةٍؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(184)\nAWALAM YATAFAKKAROO MAA BESAAHEBEHEM MIN JENNATIN IN HOWA ILLAA NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nDo they not reflect? Their companion is not seized with madness: he is but a perspicuous warner. \nاَوَلَمْ يَنْظُرُوْا فِىْ مَلَكُوْتِ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ شَىْءٍ ۙ وَّاَنْ عَسٰٓى اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ قَدِ اقْتَرَبَ اَجَلُهُمْ ۚ فَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَهٗ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(185)\nAWALAM YANZUROOA FEE MALAKOOTE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA KHALAQAL LAAHO MIN SHAY-IN WA A’SAA AN YAKOONA QADE AQTARABA AAJALUHUM FABE-AYYE HADEESIN BAA’DAH YOAMENOONA.\nDo they see nothing in the government of the heavens and the earth and all that Allah hath created? (Do they not see) that it may well be that their terms is nigh drawing to an end? In what message after this will they then believe? \nمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَلَا هَادِىَ لَهٗ ؕ وَ يَذَرُهُمْ فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(186)\nMAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FALAA HAADEAAA LAHU WA YAZARUHUM FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nTo such as Allah rejects from His guidance, there can be no guide: He will leave them in their trespasses, wandering in distraction. \nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ اَيَّانَ مُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ رَبِّىْ ۚ لَا يُجَلِّيْهَا لِوَقْتِهَاۤ اِلَّا هُوَۘ ؕؔ ثَقُلَتْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ لَا تَاْتِيْكُمْ اِلَّا بَغْتَةً  ؕ يَسْئَلُوْنَكَ كَاَنَّكَ حَفِىٌّ عَنْهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(187)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL AS-SAAA’ATE AYYAANA MURSAAHAA QUL INNAMAA I’LMOHAA I’NDAL RABBEE LAA YUJALLEEHAA LEWAQTEHAA ILLAA HOWA SAQOLAT FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ LAA TAATEEKUM ILLAA BAGHTATANW YAS-ALOONAKA KA-ANNAKA HAFEAAAUN A’NHAA QUL INNAMAA I’LMOHAA I’NDAL LAAHE LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThey ask thee about the (final) Hour - when will be its appointed time? Say: “The knowledge thereof is with my Lord (alone): None but He can reveal as to when it will occur. Heavy were its burden through the heavens and the earth. Only, all of a sudden will it come to you.” They ask thee as if thou Wert eager in search thereof: Say: “The knowledge thereof is with Allah (alone), but most men know not.” \nقُلْ لَّاۤ اَمْلِكُ لِنَفْسِىْ نَفْعًا وَّلَا ضَرًّا اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ اللّٰهُ ؕ وَلَوْ كُنْتُ اَعْلَمُ الْغَيْبَ لَاسْتَكْثَرْتُ مِنَ الْخَيْرِ ۖ ۛۚ وَمَا مَسَّنِىَ السُّۤوْءُ ۛۚ اِنْ اَنَا اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ وَّبَشِيْرٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(188)\nQUL LAA AAMLEKU LE-NAFSEE BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM ILLAA MAA SHAAA-AL LAAHO WA LAW KUNTO A-A’LAMO GHAYBA LAASTAKSARTU MENAL KHAYR WA MAA MASSANEAAA AS-SOOU IN ANAA ILLAA NAZEERUM WWABASHEERUN LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nSay: “I have no power over any good or harm to myself except as Allah willeth. If I had knowledge of the unseen, I should have multiplied all good, and no evil should have touched me: I am but a warner, and a bringer of glad tidings to those who have faith.” \nهُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ وَّجَعَلَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا لِيَسْكُنَ اِلَيْهَا ۚ فَلَمَّا تَغَشّٰٮهَا حَمَلَتْ حَمْلًا خَفِيْفًا فَمَرَّتْ بِهٖ ۚ فَلَمَّاۤ اَثْقَلَتْ دَّعَوَا اللّٰهَ رَبَّهُمَا لَئِنْ اٰتَيْتَنَا صَالِحًا لَّنَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(189)\nHOWA LAZEE KHALAQAKUM MIN NAFSIN WWAAHEDATIN ANHAARAWN MINHAA ZAWJAHAA LEESKUNA ELAYHAA FALAMMAA TAGHASSHAAHAA HAMALAT HAMLAN KHAFEEFAN FAMARRAT BEHI FALAMMAA AASQALAT DDAA’AWAA LAAHA RABBAHUMAA LAIL AAATAYTANAA SAALEHAN LLANAKOONANNA MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\n It is He Who created you from a single person, and made his mate of like nature, in order that he might dwell with her (in love). When they are united, she bears a light burden and carries it about (unnoticed). When she grows heavy, they both pray to Allah their Lord, (saying): “If Thou givest us a goodly child, we vow we shall (ever) be grateful.” \nفَلَمَّاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمَا صَالِحًا جَعَلَا لَهٗ شُرَكَآءَ فِيْمَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمَا ۚ فَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(190)\nFALAMMAA AAATAAHUMAA SAALEHAN JAA’ALAA LAHU SHORA-KAAA-A FEEMAA AAATAAHUMAA FA TA-A’ALAL LAAHO A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nBut when He giveth them a goodly child, they ascribe to others a share in the gift they have received: but Allah is exalted high above the partners they ascribe to Him. \nاَيُشْرِكُوْنَ مَا لَا يَخْلُقُ شَيْئًا وَّهُمْ يُخْلَقُوْنَ ۖ ‏(191)\nAAYUSHREKOONA MAA LAA YAKHLOQO SHAY-ANW WA HUM YUKHLAQOONA.\nDo they indeed ascribe to Him as partners things that can create nothing, but are themselves created? \nوَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ لَهُمْ نَصْرًا وَّلَاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَنْصُرُوْنَ‏(192)\nWA LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA LAHUM NASRAN WA LAA ANFOSAHUM YANSUROONA.\nNo aid can they give them, nor can they aid themselves! \nوَاِنْ تَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَى الْهُدٰى لَا يَتَّبِعُوْكُمْ ؕ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْكُمْ اَدَعَوْتُمُوْهُمْ اَمْ اَنْتُمْ صٰمِتُوْنَ‏(193)\nWA TADU’OOHUM ELAL HODAA LAA YATTABEU’OOKUM SAWAAA-UN A’LAYKUM AADAA’AWTUMOOHUM AM ANTUM SAAMETOONA.\nIf ye call them to guidance, they will not obey: For you it is the same whether ye call them or ye hold your peace! \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ عِبَادٌ اَمْثَالُكُمْ فَادْعُوْهُمْ فَلْيَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(194)\nINNAL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE E’EBAADUN AAMSAALUKUM FAADU’OOHUM FAL-YASTAJEEBOO LAKUM IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nVerily those whom ye call upon besides Allah are servants like unto you: Call upon them, and let them listen to your prayer, if ye are (indeed) truthful! \nاَلَهُمْ اَرْجُلٌ يَّمْشُوْنَ بِهَآ اَمْ لَهُمْ اَيْدٍ يَّبْطِشُوْنَ بِهَآ اَمْ لَهُمْ اَعْيُنٌ يُّبْصِرُوْنَ بِهَآ اَمْ لَهُمْ اٰذَانٌ يَّسْمَعُوْنَ بِهَا ؕ قُلِ ادْعُوْا شُرَكَآءَكُمْ ثُمَّ كِيْدُوْنِ فَلَا تُنْظِرُوْنِ‏(195)\nAALAHUM AARJULUN YYAMSHOONA BEHAA AM LAHUM AAYDIN YYABTESHOONA BEHAA AM LAHUM AAA’YUNUN YYUBSEROONA BEHAA AM LAHUM AAAZAANUN YASMA-O’ON BEHAA QOLIL O’O SHORAKAAA-AKUM SUMMA KEEDOONE FALAA TUNZEROONE.\nHave they feet to walk with? Or hands to lay hold with? Or eyes to see with? Or ears to hear with? Say: “Call your 'god-partners', scheme (your worst) against me, and give me no respite! \nاِنَّ وَلىِّۦَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ الْكِتٰبَ ۖ  وَهُوَ يَتَوَلَّى الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(196)\nINNAL WALAAAA LAAHO LAZEE NAZZALAL KETAABA WA HOWA YATAWALLAA SAALEHEEN.\n“For my Protector is Allah, Who revealed the Book (from time to time), and He will choose and befriend the righteous. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ لَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ نَصْرَكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَنْصُرُوْنَ‏(197)\nWAL LAZEENA TADU’OONA MIN DOONEHI LAA YASTATEE-O’ONA NASRAKUM WA LAA ANFOSAHUM YANSUROONA.\n“But those ye call upon besides Him, are unable to help you, and indeed to help themselves.” \nوَاِنْ تَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلَى الْهُدٰى لَا يَسْمَعُوْا ؕ وَتَرٰٮهُمْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَيْكَ وَهُمْ لَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(198)\nWA TADU’OOHUM ELAL HODAA LAA YASMAU’OOA WA TARAAHUM YANZOROONA ELAYKA WA HUM LAA YUBSEROON.\nIf thou callest them to guidance, they hear not. Thou wilt see them looking at thee, but they see not. \nخُذِ الْعَفْوَ وَاْمُرْ بِالْعُرْفِ وَاَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(199)\nKHUZE AL-A’AFWA WAAMUR BIL-U’URFE WAAA’REZ A’NIL JAAHELEEN.\nHold to forgiveness; command what is right; But turn away from the ignorant. \nوَاِمَّا يَنْزَغَنَّكَ مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ نَزْغٌ فَاسْتَعِذْ بِاللّٰهِؕ اِنَّهٗ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(200)\nWA AMMAA YANZAGHANNAKA MENAL SHAYTAANE NAZGHUN FAS-TA-I’Z BILLAAH INNAHU SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nIf a suggestion from Satan assail thy (mind), seek refuge with Allah; for He heareth and knoweth (all things). \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا اِذَا مَسَّهُمْ طٰۤئِفٌ مِّنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ تَذَكَّرُوْا فَاِذَا هُمْ مُّبْصِرُوْنَۚ‏(201)\nINNAL LAZEENA TAQAW EZAA MASSAHUM TAAEFUN MENAL SHAYTAANE TAZAKKAROOA FA-EZAA HUM MMUBSEROONA.\nThose who fear Allah, when a thought of evil from Satan assaults them, bring Allah to remembrance, when lo! they see (aright)! \nوَاِخْوَانُهُمْ يَمُدُّوْنَهُمْ فِى الْغَىِّ ثُمَّ لَا يُقْصِرُوْنَ‏(202)\nWAAKHWAANUHUM YAMUDDOONAHUM FIL GHAYY SUMMA LAA YUQSEROONA.\nBut their brethren (the evil ones) plunge them deeper into error, and never relax (their efforts). \nوَاِذَا لَمْ تَاْتِهِمْ بِاٰيَةٍ قَالُوْا لَوْلَا اجْتَبَيْتَهَا ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَتَّبِعُ مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَىَّ مِنْ رَّبِّىْ ۚ هٰذَا بَصَآئِرُ مِنْ رَّبِّكُمْ وَهُدًى وَّ رَحْمَةٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(203)\nWA EZAA LAM TAATEHEM BE-AAYATIL QAALOO LAWLAA AJTABAYTAHAA QUL INNAMAA AATTABEU’U MAA YOOHAA ELAYYA MIN A-A’LAMO HAAZAA BASAAERU MIN RABBEKUM WA HODANW WA RAHMATUN LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nIf thou bring them not a revelation, they say: “Why hast thou not got it together?” Say: “I but follow what is revealed to me from my Lord: this is (nothing but) lights from your Lord, and Guidance, and mercy, for any who have faith.” \nوَاِذَا قُرِئَ الْقُرْاٰنُ فَاسْتَمِعُوْا لَهٗ وَاَنْصِتُوْا لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(204)\nWA EZAA EZAA QUR-AANO FAASTAMEU’OOA LAHU WAANSETOOA LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nWhen the Qur'an is read, listen to it with attention, and hold your peace: that ye may receive Mercy. \nوَاذْكُرْ رَّبَّكَ فِىْ نَفْسِكَ تَضَرُّعًا وَّخِيْفَةً وَّدُوْنَ الْجَهْرِ مِنَ الْقَوْلِ بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْاٰصَالِ وَلَا تَكُنْ مِّنَ الْغٰفِلِيْنَ‏(205)\nWAAZKUR RRABBAKA FEE TUKHFEE TAZARRUA’AN WWAKHEEFATAN WWADOONA AL-JAHRE MENAL AL-QAWLE BIL-GHUDOO WAL AAASAALE WA LAA TAKUN MENAL AL-GHAAFELEENA.\nAnd do thou (O reader!) Bring thy Lord to remembrance in thy (very) soul, with humility and in reverence, without loudness in words, in the mornings and evenings; and be not thou of those who are unheedful. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُوْنَ عَنْ عِبَادَتِهٖ وَيُسَبِّحُوْنَهٗ وَلَهٗ يَسْجُدُوْنَ۩‏(206)\nINNAL LAZEENA I’NDAL RABBEKA LAA YASTAKBEROONA A’N E’EBAADATEH WAYUSABBEHOONAH WA LAHU YASJODOONA.\nThose who are near to thy Lord, disdain not to do Him worship: They celebrate His praises, and prostrate before Him. [۩] ",
  "merits": "There are 206 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. It is reported from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.), that whoever recites this Surah once a month, he will have no worry or fear on the Day of Resurrection and if it is recited on a Friday, then the reciter will be from among those who will be exempted from the taking of accounts on the Day of Judgement.\nSurah al-Aa’raaf has the Aayaat al-Mohkamaat that will give witness on behalf of its reciter on the Day of Reckoning. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that there will be a veil between the reciter of this Surah and Iblees on Judgement day and the reciter will be in the company of Prophet Adam (a.s.)\nWriting this Surah with rose water and saffron and keeping the writing at all times ensures safety from enemies and wild animals."
